<p id="S3.SS2.p6.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p6.8.1" class="ltx_text">also commutes.
Finally, the cover <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> determines an isomorphism <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{\alpha}:\det F_{\alpha}\cong\det E_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0.111em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≅</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{\alpha}:\det F_{\alpha}\cong\det E_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>. It may not agree with <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>, but since the maps below involve isomorphisms of line bundles, there exists some <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\mathcal{O}_{S}^{\times}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>×</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\mathcal{O}_{S}^{\times}(S)</annotation></semantics></math> such that the following diagram commutes</span></p><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S3.SS2.p6.pic2" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="70.09" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-33.23px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 154.15 70.09" width="154.15"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="translate(0,70.09) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(82.96,0) translate(0,33.23)"><g stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -70.77 -26.09)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 66.46)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 14.67)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 3.94 0) translate(22.13,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -16.17 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.34em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="32.34"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.SS2.p6.pic2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\det F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\det F}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 58.01 0) translate(55.44,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -16.27 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.35em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="32.54"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.SS2.p6.pic2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\det E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\det E}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 59.31)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(26.07,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -20.11 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.91em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.68" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="40.23"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.SS2.p6.pic2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\det F_{\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\det F_{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 52.15 0) translate(61.3,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -22.13 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.2em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.68" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="44.27"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.SS2.p6.pic2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\det E_{\alpha}.}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\det E_{\alpha}.}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -22.29 22.01 L 19.62 22.01"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 19.9 22.01)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -4.38 27.15)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.48em;--ltx-fo-height:0.49em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.73)" width="6.65"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.SS2.p6.pic2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.700em">ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\phi}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -44.69 13.21 L -44.69 -10.59"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 -44.69 -10.86)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -79.98 -1.38)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.32em;--ltx-fo-height:0.49em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.73)" width="32.03"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.SS2.p6.pic2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces t\cdot\det\psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">t</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.700em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.055em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">ψ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces t\cdot\det\psi}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 42.68 13.21 L 42.68 -10.59"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 42.68 -10.86)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 45.93 -1.38)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.61em;--ltx-fo-height:0.49em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.73)" width="22.28"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.SS2.p6.pic2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\det\xi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">ξ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\det\xi}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -18.35 -22.63 L 13.76 -22.63"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 14.03 -22.63)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -8.85 -17.49)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.99em;--ltx-fo-height:0.49em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.73)" width="13.66"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.SS2.p6.pic2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\phi_{\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">ϕ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\phi_{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></svg></span>
<p id="S3.SS2.p6.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p6.9.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> is rank <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> is rank <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>, this implies the diagram</span></p>
<table id="S3.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="0" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3.13)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S3.E13.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_markedasmath" height="70.09" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-33.23px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 192.45 70.09" width="192.45"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="translate(0,70.09) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(100.12,0) translate(0,33.23)"><g stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -82.68 -26.09)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 66.46)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 14.67)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 3.94 0) translate(29.05,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -23.09 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.34em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="32.34"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.E13.m1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\det F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\det F}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 69.92 0) translate(62.35,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -23.19 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.35em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="32.54"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.E13.m1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\det E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\det E}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 59.31)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(32.99,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -27.03 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.91em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.68" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="40.23"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.E13.m1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\det F_{\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\det F_{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 65.98 0) translate(66.3,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -27.13 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.92em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.68" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="40.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.E13.m1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\det E_{\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\det E_{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -20.37 22.01 L 19.62 22.01"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 19.9 22.01)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -3.42 27.15)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.48em;--ltx-fo-height:0.49em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.73)" width="6.65"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.E13.m1.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.700em">ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\phi}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -49.69 13.21 L -49.69 -10.59"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 -49.69 -10.86)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -97.14 -2.07)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.19em;--ltx-fo-height:0.62em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.18em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.06" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.63)" width="44.19"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.E13.m1.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\det(t^{2}\cdot\psi)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">t</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">ψ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\det(t^{2}\cdot\psi)}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 49.6 13.21 L 49.6 -10.59"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 49.6 -10.86)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 52.85 -1.38)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.64em;--ltx-fo-height:0.53em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.18em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.69" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.26)" width="36.51"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.E13.m1.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\det(t\cdot\xi)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">t</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">ξ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\det(t\cdot\xi)}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -16.42 -22.63 L 15.68 -22.63"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 15.95 -22.63)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -6.93 -17.49)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.99em;--ltx-fo-height:0.49em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.73)" width="13.66"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.E13.m1.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\phi_{\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">ϕ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\phi_{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></svg></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p6.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p6.10.1" class="ltx_text">also commutes. Thus, the pair of isomorphisms
<math id="S3.SS2.p6.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\cdot\xi:E\to E_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\cdot\xi:E\to E_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{2}\cdot\psi:F\to F_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{2}\cdot\psi:F\to F_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>
determine an arrow <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(E,F,\phi,\eta)\to(E_{\alpha},F_{\alpha},\phi_{\alpha},\eta_{\alpha})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(E,F,\phi,\eta)\to(E_{\alpha},F_{\alpha},\phi_{\alpha},\eta_{\alpha})</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.3. </span>The category of regular pentagonal covers</h3>

<div id="S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By the Casnati–Ekedahl theorem, each degree <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> Gorenstein cover <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha:X\to S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha:X\to S</annotation></semantics></math> determines a resolution</p>
<table id="S3.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3.14)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\rightarrow\gamma^{*}\det E_{\alpha}(-5)\rightarrow\gamma^{*}(F_{\alpha}^{\vee}\otimes\det E_{\alpha})(-3)\xrightarrow{\delta_{\alpha}}\gamma^{*}F_{\alpha}(-2)\rightarrow\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}}\rightarrow\mathcal{O}_{X}\rightarrow 0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi><mo>∨</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.055em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">δ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">α</mi></msub></mover><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\rightarrow\gamma^{*}\det E_{\alpha}(-5)\rightarrow\gamma^{*}(F_{\alpha}^{\vee}\otimes\det E_{\alpha})(-3)\xrightarrow{\delta_{\alpha}}\gamma^{*}F_{\alpha}(-2)\rightarrow\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}}\rightarrow\mathcal{O}_{X}\rightarrow 0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> has rank <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> has rank <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math>.
Casnati showed that the map <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> is alternating in the sense that it can be identified with a section of <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\wedge^{2}\pi^{*}F_{\alpha}\otimes\gamma^{*}\det E_{\alpha}^{\vee}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∧</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi><mo>∨</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\wedge^{2}\pi^{*}F_{\alpha}\otimes\gamma^{*}\det E_{\alpha}^{\vee}(1)</annotation></semantics></math>. For any pair of vector bundles <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>, via push-pull, we have an identification</p>
<table id="S3.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3.15)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Phi:H^{0}(S,\mathcal{H}om(E^{\vee}\otimes\det E,\wedge^{2}F))\xrightarrow{\sim}H^{0}(\mathbb{P}E^{\vee},\gamma^{*}(\wedge^{2}F\otimes\det E^{\vee})(1))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>E</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em">∧</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo></mover><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em">∧</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi:H^{0}(S,\mathcal{H}om(E^{\vee}\otimes\det E,\wedge^{2}F))\xrightarrow{\sim}H^{0}(\mathbb{P}E^{\vee},\gamma^{*}(\wedge^{2}F\otimes\det E^{\vee})(1)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Hence, <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to a map <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\eta_{\alpha}:=\Phi^{-1}(\delta_{\alpha}):E_{\alpha}^{\vee}\otimes\det E_{\alpha}\to\wedge^{2}F_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi><mo>∨</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em" stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em">∧</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\alpha}:=\Phi^{-1}(\delta_{\alpha}):E_{\alpha}^{\vee}\otimes\det E_{\alpha}\to\wedge^{2}F_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>. Throughout this section we shall write <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E^{\prime}:=E^{\vee}\otimes\det E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E^{\prime}:=E^{\vee}\otimes\det E</annotation></semantics></math>.
A degree <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> cover <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha:X\to S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha:X\to S</annotation></semantics></math> is called <em id="S3.SS3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">regular</em> if <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> is injective as a map of vector bundles (i.e. the cokernel of <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> is locally free). Casnati notes that if <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha^{-1}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha^{-1}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> is a local complete intersection scheme for all <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in S</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> is regular, so all covers we need will be regular. We let <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Pent}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pent</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Pent}(S)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the category whose objects are regular, degree <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> Gorenstein covers <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha:X\to S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha:X\to S</annotation></semantics></math> and arrows are isomorphisms over <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Regular degree <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> covers have a nice geometric description. Indeed, if the cover is regular, then <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to an injective map <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="E^{\prime}_{\alpha}\rightarrow\wedge^{2}F_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>α</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mo lspace="0em">∧</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>F</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E^{\prime}_{\alpha}\rightarrow\wedge^{2}F_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, which induces an embedding</p>
<table id="S3.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3.16)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}E_{\alpha}^{\prime}\hookrightarrow\mathbb{P}(\wedge^{2}F_{\alpha})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em">∧</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}E_{\alpha}^{\prime}\hookrightarrow\mathbb{P}(\wedge^{2}F_{\alpha}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Given a section <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\delta\in H^{0}(\mathbb{P}E^{\vee},\gamma^{*}(\wedge^{2}F\otimes\det E^{\vee})(1))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em">∧</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in H^{0}(\mathbb{P}E^{\vee},\gamma^{*}(\wedge^{2}F\otimes\det E^{\vee})(1))</annotation></semantics></math>, we let <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(\delta)\subset\mathbb{P}E^{\vee}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(\delta)\subset\mathbb{P}E^{\vee}</annotation></semantics></math> be the subscheme defined by the vanishing of <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\times 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\times 4</annotation></semantics></math> Pfaffians of <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>. When <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> is regular, we can recover <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=D(\delta_{\alpha})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=D(\delta_{\alpha})</annotation></semantics></math>, which is also the same as the scheme defined by the <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\times 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\times 3</annotation></semantics></math> minors of <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> (Proposition 3.5 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite>). These <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\times 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\times 3</annotation></semantics></math> minors are pullbacks to <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}E_{\alpha}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}E_{\alpha}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> along (<a href="#S3.E16" title="In 3.3. The category of regular pentagonal covers ‣ 3. The Casnati–Ekedahl structure theorem ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.16</span></a>) of the equations that define the Grassmannian bundle <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="G(2,F_{\alpha})\subset\mathbb{P}(\wedge^{2}F_{\alpha})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em">∧</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(2,F_{\alpha})\subset\mathbb{P}(\wedge^{2}F_{\alpha})</annotation></semantics></math> under its relative Plücker embedding. Using a resolution of the relative Grassmannian, Casnati obtains another resolution of <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{X}</annotation></semantics></math> in equation (3.5.2) of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite>.
Comparing this resolution with (<a href="#S3.E14" title="In 3.3. The category of regular pentagonal covers ‣ 3. The Casnati–Ekedahl structure theorem ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.14</span></a>), the uniqueness of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmthm2" title="Theorem 3.2 (Casnati–Ekedahl, Theorem 2.1 of []). ‣ 3. The Casnati–Ekedahl structure theorem ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a> (2) induces a distinguished isomorphism <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon:F_{\alpha}\otimes\det F_{\alpha}^{\vee}\otimes(\det E_{\alpha})^{\otimes 2}\to F_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi><mo>∨</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon:F_{\alpha}\otimes\det F_{\alpha}^{\vee}\otimes(\det E_{\alpha})^{\otimes 2}\to F_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> (see p. 467 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite>). Moreover, both of these vector bundles arise as subbundles of <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sym^{2}E_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Sym</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sym^{2}E_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> and the projectivization of <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> induces the identity on points (as it must be the restriction of the identity on <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(\Sym^{2}E_{\alpha})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Sym</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(\Sym^{2}E_{\alpha})</annotation></semantics></math>).
Hence, we obtain an isomorphism of line bundles</p>
<table id="S3.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}F_{\alpha}}(1)\otimes\det F_{\alpha}^{\vee}\otimes(\det E_{\alpha})^{\otimes 2}\cong\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}(F_{\alpha}\otimes\det F_{\alpha}^{\vee}\otimes\det E_{\alpha}^{2})}(1)\cong\epsilon^{*}\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}F_{\alpha}}(1)=\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}F_{\alpha}}(1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊗</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.055em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi><mo>∨</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi><mo>∨</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}F_{\alpha}}(1)\otimes\det F_{\alpha}^{\vee}\otimes(\det E_{\alpha})^{\otimes 2}\cong\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}(F_{\alpha}\otimes\det F_{\alpha}^{\vee}\otimes\det E_{\alpha}^{2})}(1)\cong\epsilon^{*}\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}F_{\alpha}}(1)=\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}F_{\alpha}}(1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">which induces a distinguished isomorphism <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{\alpha}:(\det E_{\alpha})^{\otimes 2}\cong\det F_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.1389em">≅</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{\alpha}:(\det E_{\alpha})^{\otimes 2}\cong\det F_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Now we define a category <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Pent}^{\prime}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Pent</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Pent}^{\prime}(S)</annotation></semantics></math> that keeps track of the associated linear algebraic data of regular degree <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> covers.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 3.7</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose we are given vector bundles <math id="S3.Thmthm7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmthm7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S3.Thmthm7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> of ranks <math id="S3.Thmthm7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmthm7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S3.Thmthm7.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\eta\in H^{0}(S,\mathcal{H}om(E^{\prime},\wedge^{2}F))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em">∧</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\in H^{0}(S,\mathcal{H}om(E^{\prime},\wedge^{2}F))</annotation></semantics></math> be a global section. We say
<math id="S3.Thmthm7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> has the <em id="S3.Thmthm7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">right codimension</em> if every fiber of <math id="S3.Thmthm7.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(\Phi(\eta))\subset\mathbb{P}E^{\vee}\to S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(\Phi(\eta))\subset\mathbb{P}E^{\vee}\to S</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S3.Thmthm7.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional and <math id="S3.Thmthm7.p1.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\eta:E^{\prime}\to\wedge^{2}F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>E</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mo lspace="0em">∧</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta:E^{\prime}\to\wedge^{2}F</annotation></semantics></math> is injective with locally free cokernel.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We define <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Pent}^{\prime}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Pent</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Pent}^{\prime}(S)</annotation></semantics></math> to be the category whose objects are tuples <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(E,F,\phi,\eta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(E,F,\phi,\eta)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> are vector bundles on <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> of ranks <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> respectively, <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> is an isomorphism <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\det E)^{\otimes 2}\cong\det F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.1389em">≅</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\det E)^{\otimes 2}\cong\det F</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\eta\in H^{0}(S,\mathcal{H}om(E^{\vee}\otimes\det E,\wedge^{2}F))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>E</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em">∧</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\in H^{0}(S,\mathcal{H}om(E^{\vee}\otimes\det E,\wedge^{2}F))</annotation></semantics></math> has the right codimension.
An arrow <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(E_{1},F_{1},\phi_{1},\eta_{1})\to(E_{2},F_{2},\phi_{2},\eta_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(E_{1},F_{1},\phi_{1},\eta_{1})\to(E_{2},F_{2},\phi_{2},\eta_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Pent}^{\prime}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Pent</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Pent}^{\prime}(S)</annotation></semantics></math> is pair of isomorphisms <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi:E_{1}\to E_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi:E_{1}\to E_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi:F_{1}\to F_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi:F_{1}\to F_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> such that the following two diagrams commute</p><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S3.SS3.p4.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="71.84" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-35.92px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 163.12 71.84" width="163.12"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="translate(0,71.84) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(105.53,0) translate(0,35.92)"><g stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -53.36 -28.78)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 71.84)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 16.33)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(14.57,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -8.61 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.24em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.48" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.4)" width="17.22"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.SS3.p4.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces E_{1}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces E_{1}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 29.13 0) translate(55.4,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -16.23 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.35em;--ltx-fo-height:0.81em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.34" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.26)" width="32.46"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.SS3.p4.pic1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\wedge^{2}F_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∧</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>F</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\wedge^{2}F_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 64.7)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(14.57,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -8.61 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.24em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.48" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.4)" width="17.22"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.SS3.p4.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces E_{2}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces E_{2}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 29.13 0) translate(55.4,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -16.23 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.35em;--ltx-fo-height:0.81em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.34" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.26)" width="32.46"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.SS3.p4.pic1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\wedge^{2}F_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∧</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>F</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\wedge^{2}F_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -38.79 12.18 L -38.79 -12.48"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 -38.79 -12.76)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -102.55 -3.54)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:4.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.62em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.18em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.06" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.63)" width="60.51"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.SS3.p4.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\det\xi\otimes(\xi^{-1})^{\vee}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">ξ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">ξ</mi><mrow><mo mathsize="0.710em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.710em">∨</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\det\xi\otimes(\xi^{-1})^{\vee}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -23.95 23.05 L 8.15 23.05"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 8.43 23.05)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -13.17 28.19)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.8em;--ltx-fo-height:0.3em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="6.05" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.17)" width="11.1"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.SS3.p4.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\eta_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">η</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\eta_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 31.17 12.18 L 31.17 -11.62"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 31.17 -11.9)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 34.43 -3.38)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.46em;--ltx-fo-height:0.62em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="10.52" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.63)" width="20.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.SS3.p4.pic1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\wedge^{2}\psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">∧</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn mathsize="0.710em">2</mn></msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">ψ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\wedge^{2}\psi}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -23.95 -25.32 L 8.15 -25.32"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 8.43 -25.32)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -13.17 -20.18)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.8em;--ltx-fo-height:0.3em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="6.05" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.17)" width="11.1"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.SS3.p4.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\eta_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">η</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\eta_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></svg></span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S3.SS3.p4.pic2" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="73.82" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-35.92px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 170.88 73.82" width="170.88"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="translate(0,73.82) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(93.82,0) translate(0,35.92)"><g stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -73.41 -28.78)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 71.84)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 16.33)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(29.65,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -23.7 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.43em;--ltx-fo-height:0.81em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.34" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.26)" width="47.39"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.SS3.p4.pic2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\det E_{1}^{\otimes 2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\det E_{1}^{\otimes 2}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 61.23 0) translate(58.44,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -19.28 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.79em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.68" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="38.55"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.SS3.p4.pic2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\det F_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\det F_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 64.7)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(29.65,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -23.7 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.43em;--ltx-fo-height:0.81em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.34" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.26)" width="47.39"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.SS3.p4.pic2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\det E_{2}^{\otimes 2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\det E_{2}^{\otimes 2}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 59.31 0) translate(60.36,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -21.2 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.06em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.68" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="42.4"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.SS3.p4.pic2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\det F_{2}.}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\det F_{2}.}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -43.76 12.18 L -43.76 -11.62"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 -43.76 -11.9)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -90.84 -3.18)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.17em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.18em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.21" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.79)" width="43.82"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.SS3.p4.pic2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces(\det\xi)^{\otimes 2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">ξ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.710em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mn mathsize="0.710em">2</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces(\det\xi)^{\otimes 2}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -13.83 23.05 L 20.19 23.05"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.47 23.05)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -2.57 28.19)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.87em;--ltx-fo-height:0.49em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.73)" width="12.05"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.SS3.p4.pic2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\phi_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">ϕ</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\phi_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 46.26 12.18 L 46.26 -13.28"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 46.26 -13.55)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 49.51 -3.25)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.78em;--ltx-fo-height:0.49em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.73)" width="24.57"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.SS3.p4.pic2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\det\psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">ψ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\det\psi}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -13.83 -25.32 L 18.27 -25.32"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 18.55 -25.32)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -3.53 -20.18)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.87em;--ltx-fo-height:0.49em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.73)" width="12.05"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.SS3.p4.pic2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\phi_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">ϕ</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\phi_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></svg></span>
<p id="S3.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">There is a functor <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Pent}(S)\to\mathrm{Pent}^{\prime}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Pent</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Pent</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Pent}(S)\to\mathrm{Pent}^{\prime}(S)</annotation></semantics></math> that sends <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha:X\to S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha:X\to S</annotation></semantics></math> to the tuple <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(E_{\alpha},F_{\alpha},\phi_{\alpha},\eta_{\alpha})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(E_{\alpha},F_{\alpha},\phi_{\alpha},\eta_{\alpha})</annotation></semantics></math>. There is also a functor <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Pent}^{\prime}(S)\to\mathrm{Pent}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Pent</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>Pent</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Pent}^{\prime}(S)\to\mathrm{Pent}(S)</annotation></semantics></math> that sends a tuple <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(E,F,\phi,\eta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(E,F,\phi,\eta)</annotation></semantics></math> to the degree <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> cover <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(\Phi(\eta))\subset\mathbb{P}E^{\vee}\to S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(\Phi(\eta))\subset\mathbb{P}E^{\vee}\to S</annotation></semantics></math>. The following is essentially a restatement of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>, Theorem 3.8]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3.8</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Casnati)<span id="S3.Thmthm8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The above functors define an equivalence of categories <math id="S3.Thmthm8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Pent}(S)\cong\mathrm{Pent}^{\prime}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Pent</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Pent</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Pent}(S)\cong\mathrm{Pent}^{\prime}(S)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">The fact that <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Pent}(S)\to\mathrm{Pent}^{\prime}(S)\to\mathrm{Pent}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Pent</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Pent</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>Pent</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Pent}(S)\to\mathrm{Pent}^{\prime}(S)\to\mathrm{Pent}(S)</annotation></semantics></math> is equivalent to the identity was established by Casnati. We provide further details here that <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Pent}^{\prime}(S)\to\mathrm{Pent}(S)\to\mathrm{Pent}^{\prime}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Pent</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>Pent</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Pent</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Pent}^{\prime}(S)\to\mathrm{Pent}(S)\to\mathrm{Pent}^{\prime}(S)</annotation></semantics></math> is naturally isomorphic to the identity on <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Pent}^{\prime}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Pent</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Pent}^{\prime}(S)</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(E,F,\phi,\eta)\in\mathrm{Pent}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Pent</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(E,F,\phi,\eta)\in\mathrm{Pent}(S)</annotation></semantics></math> be given and let <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=D(\Phi(\eta))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=D(\Phi(\eta))</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha:X\to S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha:X\to S</annotation></semantics></math>.
By (3.5.2) of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite>, <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{X}</annotation></semantics></math> admits a resolution</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 0\rightarrow\gamma^{*}(\det F^{-2}\otimes\det E^{5}(-5)\rightarrow\gamma^{*}(F^{\vee}\otimes\det F^{-1}\otimes\det E^{3})(-3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.055em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mrow><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.055em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.055em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 0\rightarrow\gamma^{*}(\det F^{-2}\otimes\det E^{5}(-5)\rightarrow\gamma^{*}(F^{\vee}\otimes\det F^{-1}\otimes\det E^{3})(-3)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\qquad\qquad\rightarrow\gamma^{*}(F\otimes\det F^{-1}\otimes\det E^{2})(-2)\rightarrow\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}E^{\vee}}\rightarrow\mathcal{O}_{X}\rightarrow 0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="6.278em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.055em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.055em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\qquad\qquad\rightarrow\gamma^{*}(F\otimes\det F^{-1}\otimes\det E^{2})(-2)\rightarrow\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}E^{\vee}}\rightarrow\mathcal{O}_{X}\rightarrow 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> be the image of <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma^{*}(F\otimes\det F^{-1}\otimes\det E^{2})(-2)\to\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}E^{\vee}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma^{*}(F\otimes\det F^{-1}\otimes\det E^{2})(-2)\to\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}E^{\vee}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
When we push forward the above equation by <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\rightarrow\mathcal{O}_{S}\rightarrow\alpha_{*}\mathcal{O}_{X}\rightarrow R^{1}\gamma_{*}A_{1}\rightarrow 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\rightarrow\mathcal{O}_{S}\rightarrow\alpha_{*}\mathcal{O}_{X}\rightarrow R^{1}\gamma_{*}A_{1}\rightarrow 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">We use a similar method as in Remark <a href="#S3.Thmthm3" title="Remark 3.3. ‣ 3. The Casnati–Ekedahl structure theorem ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> to produce isomorphisms</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\alpha}\cong R^{1}\gamma_{*}A_{1}\cong R^{2}\gamma_{*}A_{2}\cong R^{3}\gamma_{*}(\gamma^{*}(\det F^{-2}\otimes\det E^{5}))(-5)\cong\det F^{-2}\det E^{4}\otimes E^{\vee}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.055em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≅</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\alpha}\cong R^{1}\gamma_{*}A_{1}\cong R^{2}\gamma_{*}A_{2}\cong R^{3}\gamma_{*}(\gamma^{*}(\det F^{-2}\otimes\det E^{5}))(-5)\cong\det F^{-2}\det E^{4}\otimes E^{\vee}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">Using <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>, we turn this into an isomorphism <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\alpha}^{\vee}\cong E^{\vee}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi><mo>∨</mo></msubsup><mo>≅</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\alpha}^{\vee}\cong E^{\vee}</annotation></semantics></math>, which we dualize to define <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi:E\cong E_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>≅</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi:E\cong E_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Using the uniqueness of the CE resolution, we also get an isomorphism <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\otimes\det F^{-1}\otimes\det E^{2}\to F_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\otimes\det F^{-1}\otimes\det E^{2}\to F_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>. Making use of <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> again, we obtain an isomorphism <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi:F\cong F_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>≅</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi:F\cong F_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>. This in turn induces a map <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(2,F)\to G(2,F_{\alpha})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(2,F)\to G(2,F_{\alpha})</annotation></semantics></math> which sends <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the points of <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> span each fiber of <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}E^{\prime}\cong\mathbb{P}E_{\alpha}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}E^{\prime}\cong\mathbb{P}E_{\alpha}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, the following diagram of linear maps of spaces commutes</span></p><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S3.SS3.p5.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="74.61" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-37.3px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 143.51 74.61" width="143.51"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="translate(0,74.61) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(71.76,0) translate(0,37.3)"><g stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -71.76 -28.78)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 74.61)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 16.33)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 2 0) translate(18.11,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -12.16 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.76em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="10.4" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.4)" width="24.31"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.SS3.p5.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathbb{P}E^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathbb{P}E^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 46.09 0) translate(62.38,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -23.22 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.36em;--ltx-fo-height:0.81em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="14.72" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.26)" width="46.43"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.SS3.p5.pic1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathbb{P}(\wedge^{2}F)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em">∧</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathbb{P}(\wedge^{2}F)}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 66.09)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(20.11,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -14.16 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.05em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.48" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.4)" width="28.31"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.SS3.p5.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathbb{P}E_{\alpha}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathbb{P}E_{\alpha}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 40.23 0) translate(68.25,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -29.08 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:4.2em;--ltx-fo-height:0.81em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="14.72" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.26)" width="58.16"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.SS3.p5.pic1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathbb{P}(\wedge^{2}F_{\alpha}).}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em">∧</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathbb{P}(\wedge^{2}F_{\alpha}).}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -51.64 15.64 L -51.64 -12.48"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 -51.64 -12.76)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -33.25 24.44 L 6.72 24.44"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 6.99 24.44)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 36.72 12.18 L 36.72 -11.62"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 36.72 -11.9)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -31.25 -25.32 L 0.85 -25.32"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 1.13 -25.32)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g></g></g></svg></span>
<p id="S3.SS3.p5.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p5.5.1" class="ltx_text">In other words, there exists <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\mathcal{O}_{S}^{\times}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>×</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\mathcal{O}_{S}^{\times}(S)</annotation></semantics></math> such that the first diagram below commutes, and, since <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> has rank <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math>, so does the second:</span></p>
<table id="S3.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

