<div id="S3.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, we must compare <math id="S3.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since all the maps involved are isomorphisms of line bundles, there exists some <math id="S3.SS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{O}_{S}^{\times}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>×</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{O}_{S}^{\times}(S)</annotation></semantics></math> such that the first diagram below commutes; recalling that <math id="S3.SS3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> is rank <math id="S3.SS3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> is rank <math id="S3.SS3.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math>, hence so does the second:</span></p><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S3.SS3.p6.pic1" class="ltx