<p id="S4.I1.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">together with an isomorphism <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi:F^{*}E\rightarrow E^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi:F^{*}E\rightarrow E^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We define <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{r,d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{r,d}</annotation></semantics></math> to be the <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\SL_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>SL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\SL_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> quotient of <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{r,d}^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>†</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{r,d}^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math>. Explicitly, the objects of <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{r,d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{r,d}</annotation></semantics></math> are triples <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(S,V,E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S,V,E)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-scheme, <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> is a rank <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> vector bundle on <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> with trivial determinant, and <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> is a rank <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> vector bundle on <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}V</annotation></semantics></math> whose restrictions to the fibers of <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}V\rightarrow S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}V\rightarrow S</annotation></semantics></math> are globally generated of degree <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>. A morphism between objects <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(S,V,E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S,V,E)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(S^{\prime},V^{\prime},E^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S^{\prime},V^{\prime},E^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> is a Cartesian diagram</p>
<table id="S4.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
