</div>
<div id="S4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Bolognesi–Vistoli gave a presentation for <math id="S4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{r,d}^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>†</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{r,d}^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math> as a quotient stack, which we briefly summarize here. Let <math id="S4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{r,d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{r,d}</annotation></semantics></math> be the affine space that represents the functor which sends a scheme <math id="S4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> to the set of matrices of size <math id="S4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(r+d)\times d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(r+d)\times d</annotation></semantics></math> with entries in <math id="S4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{0}(\mathbb{P}^{1}_{S},\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{1}_{S}}(1))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{0}(\mathbb{P}^{1}_{S},\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{1}_{S}}(1))</annotation></semantics></math>. We can identify such a matrix with the associated map</p>
<table id="S4.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{1}_{S}}(-1)^{d}\rightarrow\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{1}_{S}}^{r+d}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{1}_{S}}(-1)^{d}\rightarrow\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{1}_{S}}^{r+d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{r,d}\subset M_{r,d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{r,d}\subset M_{r,d}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the open subscheme parametrizing injective maps with locally free cokernel. The group <math id="S4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\GL_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>GL</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\GL_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> acts <math id="S4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{r,d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{r,d}</annotation></semantics></math> by multiplication on the left, <math id="S4.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\GL_{r+d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>GL</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\GL_{r+d}</annotation></semantics></math> by multiplication on the right. Bolognesi–Vistoli establish <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>, Theorem 4.4]</cite> that</p>
<table id="S4.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{r,d}^{\dagger}\cong[\Omega_{r,d}/\GL_{d}\times\GL_{d+r}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>GL</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>GL</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{r,d}^{\dagger}\cong[\Omega_{r,d}/\GL_{d}\times\GL_{d+r}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p2.3" class="ltx_p">The group <math id="S4.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\SL_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>SL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\SL_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> acts by change of coordinates on <math id="S4.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{0}(\mathbb{P}^{1}_{S},\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{1}_{S}}(1))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{0}(\mathbb{P}^{1}_{S},\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{1}_{S}}(1))</annotation></semantics></math>. This commutes with the <math id="S4.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\GL_{d}\times\GL_{d+r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>GL</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>GL</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\GL_{d}\times\GL_{d+r}</annotation></semantics></math> action. Thus we obtain the following.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmthm2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmthm2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 4.2</span></span><span id="S4.Thmthm2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmthm2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmthm2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmthm2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There is an isomorphism of fibered categories</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{r,d}\cong[\mathcal{V}_{r,d}^{\dagger}/\SL_{2}]\cong[\Omega_{r,d}/\GL_{d}\times\GL_{r+d}\times\SL_{2}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>SL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>GL</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>GL</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>SL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{r,d}\cong[\mathcal{V}_{r,d}^{\dagger}/\SL_{2}]\cong[\Omega_{r,d}/\GL_{d}\times\GL_{r+d}\times\SL_{2}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmthm3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmthm3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 4.3</span></span><span id="S4.Thmthm3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmthm3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmthm3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Bolognesi–Vistoli also describe the <math id="S4.Thmthm3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\PGL_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>PGL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\PGL_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> quotient of <math id="S4.Thmthm3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{r,d}^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>†</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{r,d}^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is slightly more subtle. This distinction is important in their work which concerns <em id="S4.Thmthm3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">integral</em> coefficients.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To parametrize the linear algebraic data associated to a low degree cover of <math id="S4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we are interested in
products of the form <math id="S4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{r,d}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{s,e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>BSL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{r,d}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{s,e}</annotation></semantics></math>, which parametrize a pair of vector bundles on the same <math id="S4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-bundle. Let <math id="S4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{r,d,s,e}:=\GL_{d}\times\GL_{r+d}\times\GL_{e}\times\GL_{s+e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>GL</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>GL</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>GL</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>GL</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{r,d,s,e}:=\GL_{d}\times\GL_{r+d}\times\GL_{e}\times\GL_{s+e}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The group <math id="S4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{r,d,s,e}\times\SL_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>SL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{r,d,s,e}\times\SL_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> acts on <math id="S4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{r,d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{r,d}</annotation></semantics></math> via the projection <math id="S4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{r,d,s,e}\times\SL_{2}\to\GL_{d}\times\GL_{r+d}\times\SL_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>SL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi>GL</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>GL</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>SL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{r,d,s,e}\times\SL_{2}\to\GL_{d}\times\GL_{r+d}\times\SL_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>; and similarly on <math id="S4.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{s,e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{s,e}</annotation></semantics></math> via the projection <math id="S4.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{r,d,s,e}\times\SL_{2}\to\GL_{e}\times\GL_{s+e}\times\SL_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>SL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi>GL</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>GL</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>SL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{r,d,s,e}\times\SL_{2}\to\GL_{e}\times\GL_{s+e}\times\SL_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By Proposition <a href="#S4.Thmthm2" title="Proposition 4.2. ‣ 4. Pairs of vector bundles on 
        
          
            
            P
            1
          
        
      -bundles ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>, it follows that</p>
<table id="S4.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(4.1)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{r,d}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{s,e}=[\Omega_{r,d}\times\Omega_{s,e}/G_{r,d,s,e}\times\SL_{2}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>BSL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>SL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{r,d}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{s,e}=[\Omega_{r,d}\times\Omega_{s,e}/G_{r,d,s,e}\times\SL_{2}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{r+d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{r+d}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the universal vector bundles on <math id="S4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\BGL_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>BGL</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\BGL_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\BGL_{r+d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>BGL</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\BGL_{r+d}</annotation></semantics></math>; similarly, let <math id="S4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{e}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{s+e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{s+e}</annotation></semantics></math> be the universal vector bundles on <math id="S4.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\BGL_{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>BGL</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\BGL_{e}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\BGL_{s+e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>BGL</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\BGL_{s+e}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The Chow ring of <math id="S4.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{B}(G_{r,d,s,e}\times\SL_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>SL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{B}(G_{r,d,s,e}\times\SL_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> is the free <math id="S4.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℚ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra on the Chern classes of <math id="S4.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{d},T_{r+d},S_{e},S_{s+e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{d},T_{r+d},S_{e},S_{s+e}</annotation></semantics></math>, together with the universal second Chern class <math id="S4.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S4.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\BSL_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>BSL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\BSL_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let us denote these classes by</p>
<table id="S4.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex6.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=c_{i}(T_{d})\qquad\text{and}\qquad u_{i}=c_{i}(T_{r+d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mtext>and</mtext><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=c_{i}(T_{d})\qquad\text{and}\qquad u_{i}=c_{i}(T_{r+d})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=c_{i}(S_{e})\qquad\text{and}\qquad w_{i}=c_{i}(S_{s+e})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mtext>and</mtext><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=c_{i}(S_{e})\qquad\text{and}\qquad w_{i}=c_{i}(S_{s+e}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="S4.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{r,d}\times\Omega_{s,e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{r,d}\times\Omega_{s,e}</annotation></semantics></math> is open inside the affine space <math id="S4.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{r,d}\times M_{s,e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{r,d}\times M_{s,e}</annotation></semantics></math>,
the excision and homotopy properties imply</p>
<table id="S4.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="0" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(4.2)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><span id="S4.E2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath"><math id="S4.E2.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\mathcal{V}_{r,d}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{s,e})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>BSL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\mathcal{V}_{r,d}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{s,e})</annotation></semantics></math> is generated by the restrictions of the <math id="S4.E2.m1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i},u_{i},v_{i},w_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i},u_{i},v_{i},w_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We now identify the restrictions of the tautological bundles <math id="S4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{d+r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{d+r}</annotation></semantics></math> in terms of the universal rank <math id="S4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, degree <math id="S4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> vector bundle on <math id="S4.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="S4.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi:\mathcal{P}\rightarrow\mathcal{V}_{r,d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi:\mathcal{P}\rightarrow\mathcal{V}_{r,d}</annotation></semantics></math> be the universal <math id="S4.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-bundle. We write <math id="S4.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z:=c_{1}(\mathcal{O}_{\mathcal{P}}(1))\in A^{1}(\mathcal{P})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z:=c_{1}(\mathcal{O}_{\mathcal{P}}(1))\in A^{1}(\mathcal{P})</annotation></semantics></math>.
We have <math id="S4.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}=c_{2}(\pi_{*}\mathcal{O}_{\mathcal{P}}(1))\in A^{2}(\mathcal{V}_{r,d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}=c_{2}(\pi_{*}\mathcal{O}_{\mathcal{P}}(1))\in A^{2}(\mathcal{V}_{r,d})</annotation></semantics></math>, the universal second Chern class (pulled back via the natural map <math id="S4.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{r,d}\rightarrow\BSL_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>BSL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{r,d}\rightarrow\BSL_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>).
Note that <math id="S4.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}(\pi_{*}\mathcal{O}_{\mathcal{P}}(1))=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}(\pi_{*}\mathcal{O}_{\mathcal{P}}(1))=0</annotation></semantics></math>, so by Equation (<a href="#S2.E1" title="In 2.1. Projective bundles ‣ 2. Notation and conventions ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>),</p>
<table id="S4.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\mathcal{P})=A^{*}(\mathcal{V}_{r,d})[z]/(z^{2}+\pi^{*}c_{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\mathcal{P})=A^{*}(\mathcal{V}_{r,d})[z]/(z^{2}+\pi^{*}c_{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p5.2" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S4.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math> be the universal rank <math id="S4.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, degree <math id="S4.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> vector bundle on <math id="S4.p5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The Chern classes of <math id="S4.p5.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math> may thus be written as</p>
<table id="S4.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}(\mathcal{E})=\pi^{*}a_{i}+(\pi^{*}a_{i}^{\prime})z\qquad\text{where}\qquad a_{i}\in A^{i}(\mathcal{V}_{r,d}),\quad a_{i}^{\prime}\in A^{i-1}(\mathcal{V}_{r,d})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mtext>where</mtext><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}(\mathcal{E})=\pi^{*}a_{i}+(\pi^{*}a_{i}^{\prime})z\qquad\text{where}\qquad a_{i}\in A^{i}(\mathcal{V}_{r,d}),\quad a_{i}^{\prime}\in A^{i-1}(\mathcal{V}_{r,d}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p5.3" class="ltx_p">Note that <math id="S4.p5.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1}^{\prime}=d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1}^{\prime}=d</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S4.p5.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma:\mathcal{V}_{r,d}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{s,e}\to B(G_{r,d,s,e}\times\SL_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>BSL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>SL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma:\mathcal{V}_{r,d}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{s,e}\to B(G_{r,d,s,e}\times\SL_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> be the structure map. Then by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>, Lemma 3.2]</cite> (noting that <math id="S4.p5.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\det(\pi_{*}\mathcal{O}_{\mathcal{P}}(1))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\det(\pi_{*}\mathcal{O}_{\mathcal{P}}(1))</annotation></semantics></math> is trivial), we have</p>
<table id="S4.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(4.3)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma^{*}T_{d}=\pi_{*}\mathcal{E}(-1)\qquad\text{and}\qquad\gamma^{*}T_{r+d}=\pi_{*}\mathcal{E}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma^{*}T_{d}=\pi_{*}\mathcal{E}(-1)\qquad\text{and}\qquad\gamma^{*}T_{r+d}=\pi_{*}\mathcal{E}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p5.4" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="S4.p5.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{1}\pi_{*}\mathcal{E}(-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{1}\pi_{*}\mathcal{E}(-1)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p5.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{1}\pi_{*}\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{1}\pi_{*}\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math> are zero, Grothendieck–Riemann–Roch says that
the Chern characters of <math id="S4.p5.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{*}\mathcal{E}(-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{*}\mathcal{E}(-1)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p5.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{*}\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{*}\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math> are push forwards by <math id="S4.p5.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> of polynomials in the <math id="S4.p5.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}(\mathcal{E})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}(\mathcal{E})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p5.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math>. The push forward of such a polynomial is a polynomial in the <math id="S4.p5.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i},a_{i}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i},a_{i}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p5.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, the restrictions of <math id="S4.p5.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p5.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.p5.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\mathcal{V}_{r,d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\mathcal{V}_{r,d})</annotation></semantics></math> are polynomials in <math id="S4.p5.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1},\ldots,a_{r},a_{2}^{\prime},\ldots,a_{r}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1},\ldots,a_{r},a_{2}^{\prime},\ldots,a_{r}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p5.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1. </span>The rational Chow ring</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let us denote the universal rank <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> vector bundle from the second factor of <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{r,d}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{s,e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>BSL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{r,d}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{s,e}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math> and its Chern classes by</p>
<table id="S4.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}(\mathcal{F})=\pi^{*}b_{i}+(\pi^{*}b_{i}^{\prime})z\qquad\text{where}\qquad b_{i}\in A^{i}(\mathcal{V}_{s,e}),\quad b_{i}^{\prime}\in A^{i-1}(\mathcal{V}_{s,e})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mtext>where</mtext><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}(\mathcal{F})=\pi^{*}b_{i}+(\pi^{*}b_{i}^{\prime})z\qquad\text{where}\qquad b_{i}\in A^{i}(\mathcal{V}_{s,e}),\quad b_{i}^{\prime}\in A^{i-1}(\mathcal{V}_{s,e}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">It follows from Equation (<a href="#S4.E2" title="In 4. Pairs of vector bundles on 
        
          
            
            P
            1
          
        
      -bundles ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>) and the discussion following (applied to both factors of the product) that the <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i},a_{i}^{\prime},b_{i},b_{i}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i},a_{i}^{\prime},b_{i},b_{i}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are generators for <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\mathcal{V}_{r,d}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{s,d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>BSL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\mathcal{V}_{r,d}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{s,d})</annotation></semantics></math>. We now show that there are no relations among these generators in low degrees.
This is a generalization of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>, Theorem 4.1]</cite>, which shows <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\mathcal{V}_{r,d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\mathcal{V}_{r,d})</annotation></semantics></math> is generated by the <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i},a_{i}^{\prime}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i},a_{i}^{\prime},</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> with no relations in degrees less than <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d+1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmthm4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmthm4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 4.4</span></span><span id="S4.Thmthm4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmthm4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmthm4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmthm4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The rational Chow ring of <math id="S4.Thmthm4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{r,d}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{s,e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>BSL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{r,d}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{s,e}</annotation></semantics></math> is generated as a <math id="S4.Thmthm4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℚ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra by</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2},a_{1},\ldots,a_{r},a_{2}^{\prime},\ldots,a_{r}^{\prime},b_{1},\ldots,b_{s},b_{2}^{\prime},\ldots,b_{s}^{\prime}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2},a_{1},\ldots,a_{r},a_{2}^{\prime},\ldots,a_{r}^{\prime},b_{1},\ldots,b_{s},b_{2}^{\prime},\ldots,b_{s}^{\prime},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmthm4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmthm4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and all relations have degree at least <math id="S4.Thmthm4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min(d,e)+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min(d,e)+1</annotation></semantics></math>. In the notation of Equation (<a href="#S2.E2" title="In 2.2. (Equivariant) Intersection Theory ‣ 2. Notation and conventions ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\trun^{\min(d,e)+1}A^{*}(\mathcal{V}_{r,d}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{s,e})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Trun</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>BSL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\trun^{\min(d,e)+1}A^{*}(\mathcal{V}_{r,d}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{s,e})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\qquad=\trun^{\min(d,e)+1}\mathbb{Q}[c_{2},a_{1},\ldots,a_{r},a_{2}^{\prime},\ldots,a_{r}^{\prime},b_{1},\ldots,b_{s},b_{2}^{\prime},\ldots,b_{s}^{\prime}]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="4.278em">=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Trun</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\qquad=\trun^{\min(d,e)+1}\mathbb{Q}[c_{2},a_{1},\ldots,a_{r},a_{2}^{\prime},\ldots,a_{r}^{\prime},b_{1},\ldots,b_{s},b_{2}^{\prime},\ldots,b_{s}^{\prime}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmthm5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmthm5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 4.5</span></span><span id="S4.Thmthm5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmthm5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">(1) The codimension of the complement of <math id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{r,d}\subset M_{r,d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{r,d}\subset M_{r,d}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, so the Theorem does <em id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">not</em> follow immediately from dimension counting and excision if <math id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min(d,e)&gt;\min(r,s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min(d,e)&gt;\min(r,s)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmthm5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmthm5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">(2) If <math id="S4.Thmthm5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=0</annotation></semantics></math>, the fact that there are no <math id="S4.Thmthm5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> classes follows immediately from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>, Theorem 4.1]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M:=[M_{r,d}/G_{r,d,s,e}\times\SL_{2}]\quad\text{and}\quad N:=[M_{s,e}/G_{r,d,s,e}\times\SL_{2}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>SL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>SL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M:=[M_{r,d}/G_{r,d,s,e}\times\SL_{2}]\quad\text{and}\quad N:=[M_{s,e}/G_{r,d,s,e}\times\SL_{2}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Equation (<a href="#S4.E1" title="In 4. Pairs of vector bundles on 
        
          
            
            P
            1
          
        
      -bundles ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>) says that <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{r,d}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{s,e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>BSL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{r,d}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{s,e}</annotation></semantics></math> is an open inside the vector bundle <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\oplus N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⊕</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\oplus N</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B:=\mathrm{B}(G_{r,d,s,e}\times\SL_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>SL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B:=\mathrm{B}(G_{r,d,s,e}\times\SL_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.
The complement consists of two components, namely</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X:=[\Omega_{r,d}^{c}\times M_{s,e}/G_{r,d,s,e}\times\SL_{2}]\quad\text{and}\quad Y:=[M_{r,d}\times\Omega_{s,e}^{c}/G_{r,d,s,e}\times\SL_{2}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>SL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mi>c</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>SL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X:=[\Omega_{r,d}^{c}\times M_{s,e}/G_{r,d,s,e}\times\SL_{2}]\quad\text{and}\quad Y:=[M_{r,d}\times\Omega_{s,e}^{c}/G_{r,d,s,e}\times\SL_{2}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">One readily checks that <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\subset\mathcal{V}_{r,d}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{s,e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>BSL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\subset\mathcal{V}_{r,d}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{s,e}</annotation></semantics></math> is irreducible of codimension <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\subset\mathcal{V}_{r,d}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{s,e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>BSL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\subset\mathcal{V}_{r,d}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{s,e}</annotation></semantics></math> is irreducible of codimension <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> (see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>, Remark 4.3]</cite>).
Excision gives a right-exact sequence</span></p>
<table id="S4.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(4.4)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*-r}(X)\oplus A^{*-s}(Y)\rightarrow A^{*}(M\oplus N)\rightarrow A^{*}(\mathcal{V}_{r,d}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{s,e})\rightarrow 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⊕</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>BSL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*-r}(X)\oplus A^{*-s}(Y)\rightarrow A^{*}(M\oplus N)\rightarrow A^{*}(\mathcal{V}_{r,d}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{s,e})\rightarrow 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">From this it is clear that there are no relations among the restrictions to <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{r,d}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{s,e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>BSL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{r,d}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{s,e}</annotation></semantics></math> of the Chern classes of <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{d},T_{d+r},S_{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{d},T_{d+r},S_{e}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{s+e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{s+e}</annotation></semantics></math> in degrees less than <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min(r,s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min(r,s)</annotation></semantics></math>.
We now describe relations among the restrictions of these Chern classes in degrees <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min(r,s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min(r,s)</annotation></semantics></math> up to <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min(d,e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min(d,e)</annotation></semantics></math>. (If <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min(d,e)&lt;\min(r,s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min(d,e)&lt;\min(r,s)</annotation></semantics></math> we are already done.)
In particular, shall conclude that</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(4.5)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\trun^{\min(d,e)+1}A^{*}(\mathcal{V}_{r,d}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{s,e})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Trun</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>BSL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\trun^{\min(d,e)+1}A^{*}(\mathcal{V}_{r,d}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{s,e})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad=\trun^{\min(d,e)+1}\mathbb{Q}[c_{2},t_{1},\ldots,t_{r-1},u_{1},\ldots,u_{r},v_{1},\ldots v_{s-1},w_{1},\ldots,w_{s}]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="2.278em">=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Trun</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad=\trun^{\min(d,e)+1}\mathbb{Q}[c_{2},t_{1},\ldots,t_{r-1},u_{1},\ldots,u_{r},v_{1},\ldots v_{s-1},w_{1},\ldots,w_{s}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since the classes in the statement of the theorem are generators and have the same degrees as those above, the statement in the theorem must hold for dimension reasons.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">It suffices to understand the image of <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*-r}(X)\to A^{*}(M\oplus N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⊕</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*-r}(X)\to A^{*}(M\oplus N)</annotation></semantics></math>, the other factor being similar.
For this we resolve <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> (resp. <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>) as in the proof of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>, Theorem 4.1]</cite>, taking the <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> factor (resp. <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> factor) “along for the ride”.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using the excision sequence (<a href="#S4.E4" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.1. The rational Chow ring ‣ 4. Pairs of vector bundles on 
        
          
            
            P
            1
          
        
      -bundles ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a>) and arguing exactly as in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>, Theorem 4.1]</cite>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S4.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(4.6)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A^{*}(\mathcal{V}_{r,d}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{s,e})=\frac{\mathbb{Q}[c_{2},t_{1},\ldots,t_{d},u_{1},\ldots,u_{r+d},v_{1},\ldots,v_{e},w_{1},\ldots,w_{s+e}]}{\langle f_{i,j}:0\leq i\leq 1,0\leq j\leq d-1\rangle+\langle g_{i,j}:0\leq i\leq 1,0\leq j\leq e-1\rangle}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">A</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>BSL</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">e</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℚ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">c</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">v</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">v</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">e</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">f</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">g</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">e</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\mathcal{V}_{r,d}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{s,e})=\frac{\mathbb{Q}[c_{2},t_{1},\ldots,t_{d},u_{1},\ldots,u_{r+d},v_{1},\ldots,v_{e},w_{1},\ldots,w_{s+e}]}{\langle f_{i,j}:0\leq i\leq 1,0\leq j\leq d-1\rangle+\langle g_{i,j}:0\leq i\leq 1,0\leq j\leq e-1\rangle}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">where</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f_{1,j-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{1,j-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-t_{j+r}+u_{j+r}+\ldots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-t_{j+r}+u_{j+r}+\ldots</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f_{0,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{0,j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex17.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-(r+d)t_{j+r}+(d-j)u_{j+r}+\ldots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-(r+d)t_{j+r}+(d-j)u_{j+r}+\ldots</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle g_{1,j-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle g_{1,j-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-v_{j+s}+w_{j+s}+\ldots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-v_{j+s}+w_{j+s}+\ldots</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle g_{0,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle g_{0,j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex18.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-(s+e)v_{j+s}+(e-j)w_{j+s}+\ldots." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-(s+e)v_{j+s}+(e-j)w_{j+s}+\ldots.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, in <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\mathcal{V}_{r,d}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{s,e})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>BSL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\mathcal{V}_{r,d}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{s,e})</annotation></semantics></math>,
the classes <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\leq n\leq d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\leq n\leq d</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r+1\leq m\leq d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r+1\leq m\leq d</annotation></semantics></math> are expressible as polynomials in <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2},t_{1},\ldots,t_{r-1},u_{1},\ldots,u_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2},t_{1},\ldots,t_{r-1},u_{1},\ldots,u_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, after eliminating these higher degree generators, the <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> produce no additional relations in degrees less than or equal to <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> among the restrictions to <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{r,d}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{s,e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>BSL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{r,d}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{s,e}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2},t_{1},\ldots,t_{r-1},u_{1},\ldots,u_{r},v_{1},\ldots,v_{e},w_{1},\ldots,w_{s+e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2},t_{1},\ldots,t_{r-1},u_{1},\ldots,u_{r},v_{1},\ldots,v_{e},w_{1},\ldots,w_{s+e}</annotation></semantics></math>. With the analogous
calculation for the <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math>, equation (<a href="#S4.E6" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.1. The rational Chow ring ‣ 4. Pairs of vector bundles on 
        
          
            
            P
            1
          
        
      -bundles ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.6</span></a>) then implies (<a href="#S4.E5" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.1. The rational Chow ring ‣ 4. Pairs of vector bundles on 
        
          
            
            P
            1
          
        
      -bundles ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.5</span></a>), and hence the statement of the theorem.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2. </span>Splitting loci</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Every vector bundle <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> splits as a direct sum of line bundles, <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E\cong\mathcal{O}(e_{1})\oplus\cdots\oplus\mathcal{O}(e_{r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E\cong\mathcal{O}(e_{1})\oplus\cdots\oplus\mathcal{O}(e_{r})</annotation></semantics></math> for integers <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{1}\leq\cdots\leq e_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{1}\leq\cdots\leq e_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>. We call the non-decreasing sequence of integers <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{e}=(e_{1},\ldots,e_{r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{e}=(e_{1},\ldots,e_{r})</annotation></semantics></math> the <em id="S4.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">splitting type</em> of <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> and will often abbreviate the corresponding sum of line bundles by <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(\vec{e}):=\mathcal{O}(e_{1})\oplus\cdots\oplus\mathcal{O}(e_{r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(\vec{e}):=\mathcal{O}(e_{1})\oplus\cdots\oplus\mathcal{O}(e_{r})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Given a family of vector bundles <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math> on a <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-bundle <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi:\mathcal{P}\to B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi:\mathcal{P}\to B</annotation></semantics></math>, the base <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> is stratified by locally closed subvarieties</p>
<table id="S4.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{b\in B:\mathcal{E}_{\pi^{-1}(b)}\cong\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{b\in B:\mathcal{E}_{\pi^{-1}(b)}\cong\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">which we call the <em id="S4.SS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">splitting locus for <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{e}</annotation></semantics></math></em>. A subscheme structure on splitting loci is defined in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>, Section 2]</cite>, though it will not be necessary here.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The splitting type <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{e}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> is equivalent to the data of the ranks of cohomology groups <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{0}(\mathbb{P}^{1},E(m))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{0}(\mathbb{P}^{1},E(m))</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in\mathbb{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in\mathbb{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>. Conversely, the locus of points <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\in B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\in B</annotation></semantics></math> where the fibers of <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy some cohomological condition is a union of splitting loci.
For example,
the locus in <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math> fails to be globally generated on fibers is the union of splitting loci for splitting types <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{e}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{1}\leq-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0em">≤</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{1}\leq-1</annotation></semantics></math>. Similarly, <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Supp R^{1}\pi_{*}\mathcal{E}(-2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Supp</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Supp R^{1}\pi_{*}\mathcal{E}(-2)</annotation></semantics></math> is the union of all splitting loci with <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{1}\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{1}\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Following the argument in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>, Lemma 5.1]</cite>, the codimension in <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{r,d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{r,d}</annotation></semantics></math> of the splitting locus where the universal <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{r,d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{r,d}</annotation></semantics></math> has splitting type <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{e}</annotation></semantics></math> on fibers of <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}\to\mathcal{V}_{r,d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}\to\mathcal{V}_{r,d}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{E}nd(\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{E}nd(\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})))</annotation></semantics></math>.
If we have a <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-bundle equipped with two vector bundles, we can consider the intersections of splitting loci for both bundles.
The simultaneous splitting locus in <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{r,d}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{s,e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>BSL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{r,d}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{s,e}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math> has splitting type <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{e}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> has splitting type <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{f}</annotation></semantics></math> is equal to the product of the <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{e}</annotation></semantics></math> splitting locus in <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{r,d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{r,d}</annotation></semantics></math> with the <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{f}</annotation></semantics></math> splitting locus in <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{s,e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{s,e}</annotation></semantics></math>, and therefore
has codimension</p>
<table id="S4.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(4.7)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{E}nd(\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})))+h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{E}nd(\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{E}nd(\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})))+h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{E}nd(\mathcal{O}(\vec{f}))).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5. </span>The good opens and codimension bounds</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each <math id="S5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=3,4,5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=3,4,5</annotation></semantics></math> and genus <math id="S5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>, we will define a stack <math id="S5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{k,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{k,g}</annotation></semantics></math> parametrizing the vector bundles associated to a degree <math id="S5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, genus <math id="S5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> cover of <math id="S5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. The stack <math id="S5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{k,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{k,g}</annotation></semantics></math> will come equipped with a universal <math id="S5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-bundle <math id="S5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi:\mathcal{P}\to\mathcal{B}_{k,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi:\mathcal{P}\to\mathcal{B}_{k,g}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we will define a vector bundle <math id="S5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{k,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{k,g}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math> whose sections on a fiber of <math id="S5.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}\to\mathcal{B}_{k,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}\to\mathcal{B}_{k,g}</annotation></semantics></math> is the relevant space of sections in the linear algebraic data of covers appearing in Section <a href="#S3" title="3. The Casnati–Ekedahl structure theorem ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Before treating the case for each <math id="S5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> in depth, we briefly outline our construction of certain open substacks of the Hurwitz stack. For <math id="S5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=3</annotation></semantics></math>, we shall define <math id="S5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{3,g}^{\prime}\subseteq\mathcal{B}_{3,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{3,g}^{\prime}\subseteq\mathcal{B}_{3,g}</annotation></semantics></math> to be the open substack over which <math id="S5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{3,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{3,g}</annotation></semantics></math> is globally generated on the fibers of <math id="S5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi:\mathcal{P}\to\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi:\mathcal{P}\to\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For <math id="S5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=4,5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=4,5</annotation></semantics></math>, let us define the open substack</p>
<table id="S5.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.E1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(5.1)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{B}_{k,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{B}_{k,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\mathcal{B}_{k,g}\smallsetminus\Supp(R^{1}\pi_{*}\mathcal{U}_{k,g})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mi>Supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\mathcal{B}_{k,g}\smallsetminus\Supp(R^{1}\pi_{*}\mathcal{U}_{k,g}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p2.2" class="ltx_p">By the theorem on cohomology and base change, the restriction of <math id="S5.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{*}\mathcal{U}_{k,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{*}\mathcal{U}_{k,g}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S5.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{k,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{k,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is locally free with fibers given by the relevant space of sections in the linear algebraic data of covers appearing in Section <a href="#S3" title="3. The Casnati–Ekedahl structure theorem ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. We denote the total space of this vector bundle on <math id="S5.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{k,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{k,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> by</p>
<table id="S5.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{k,g}^{\prime}:=\pi_{*}\mathcal{U}_{k,g}|_{\mathcal{B}_{k,g}^{\prime}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{k,g}^{\prime}:=\pi_{*}\mathcal{U}_{k,g}|_{\mathcal{B}_{k,g}^{\prime}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">As discussed in Section <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2. Splitting loci ‣ 4. Pairs of vector bundles on 
        
          
            
            P
            1
          
        
      -bundles ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>, the complement of <math id="S5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{k,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{k,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is a union of splitting loci. The splitting loci in the complement are determined by the condition that <math id="S5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{k,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{k,g}</annotation></semantics></math> has a summand of degree <math id="S5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-2</annotation></semantics></math> or less.
It will also be convenient to work with a slightly smaller open substack</p>
<table id="S5.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(5.2)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{k,g}^{\circ}:=\mathcal{B}_{k,g}\smallsetminus\Supp(R^{1}\pi_{*}(\mathcal{U}_{k,g}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{\mathcal{P}}(-2)))," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mi>Supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{k,g}^{\circ}:=\mathcal{B}_{k,g}\smallsetminus\Supp(R^{1}\pi_{*}(\mathcal{U}_{k,g}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{\mathcal{P}}(-2))),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p3.2" class="ltx_p">whose complement consists of splitting loci where <math id="S5.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{k,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{k,g}</annotation></semantics></math> has a summand of degree <math id="S5.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> or less. (Having a cut-off in terms of a degree <math id="S5.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> summand will be cleaner than a cut-off in terms of a <math id="S5.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-2</annotation></semantics></math> summand for our next step of bounding the codimension of the complement. The open <math id="S5.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{k,g}^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{k,g}^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math> also plays an important role in our sequel <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite>, where
the slightly stronger positivity condition on the fibers of <math id="S5.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{k,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{k,g}</annotation></semantics></math> will be needed.)</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Pulling back these open substacks along the natural map <math id="S5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k,g}\to\mathcal{B}_{k,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k,g}\to\mathcal{B}_{k,g}</annotation></semantics></math> defines open substacks of the Hurwitz space as in the diagram below</p>
<table id="S5.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="0" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(5.3)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S5.E3.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_markedasmath" height="73.89" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-36.94px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 259.15 73.89" width="259.15"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="translate(0,73.89) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(129.58,0) translate(0,36.94)"><g stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -129.58 -27.92)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 73.88)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 15.47)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(42.92,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -36.96 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:4.34em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.57" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="60.08"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.E3.m1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\circ}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\circ}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 85.84 0) translate(59.12,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -19.95 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.88em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="14.36" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.4)" width="26.06"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.E3.m1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 172.5 0) translate(59.12,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -19.95 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.88em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.41" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="26.06"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.E3.m1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{H}_{k,g}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{H}_{k,g}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 64.87)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 17.3 0) translate(25.62,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -19.66 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.84em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.49" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.53)" width="25.49"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.E3.m1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{B}_{k,g}^{\circ}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{B}_{k,g}^{\circ}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 86.12 0) translate(58.83,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -19.66 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.84em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="14.36" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.4)" width="25.49"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.E3.m1.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{B}_{k,g}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{B}_{k,g}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 170.86 0) translate(60.75,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -21.58 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.12em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.41" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="29.33"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.E3.m1.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{B}_{k,g}.}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{B}_{k,g}.}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -86.66 12.18 L -86.66 -12.5"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 -86.66 -12.77)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -43.46 24.94 L -11.36 24.94"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -11.09 24.94)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 15.38 12.18 L 15.38 -11.62"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 15.38 -11.9)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 41.56 24.94 L 75.3 24.94"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 75.57 24.94)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 102.03 12.18 L 102.03 -12.57"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 102.03 -12.85)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -60.76 -24.46 L -11.07 -24.46"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -10.8 -24.46)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 41.27 -24.46 L 73.66 -24.46"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 73.94 -24.46)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g></g></g></svg></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p4.2" class="ltx_p">In all cases, we shall see that <math id="S5.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is an open substack inside the vector bundle <math id="S5.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{k,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{k,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S5.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{k,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{k,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, we will find that the Chow ring of <math id="S5.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is generated by tautological classes. To turn this into meaningful results for the Chow ring of <math id="S5.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k,g}</annotation></semantics></math> we must describe the complement of <math id="S5.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\prime}\subseteq\mathcal{H}_{k,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\prime}\subseteq\mathcal{H}_{k,g}</annotation></semantics></math>.
When <math id="S5.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=3</annotation></semantics></math>, it turns out <math id="S5.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\prime}=\mathcal{H}_{k,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\prime}=\mathcal{H}_{k,g}</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="S5.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=4</annotation></semantics></math>, the complement of <math id="S5.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> contains covers that factor through an intermediate curve of low genus. Nevertheless, we show that the complement of <math id="S5.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> intersects <math id="S5.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\mathrm{nf}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>nf</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\mathrm{nf}}</annotation></semantics></math> in high codimension.
Finally, for <math id="S5.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=5</annotation></semantics></math>, we show that the complement of <math id="S5.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{5,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{5,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> has high codimension.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Of course, the complement of <math id="S5.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is contained in the complement of <math id="S5.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math>, so it will suffice to bound the codimension of the complement of <math id="S5.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math> (which in turn provides a lower bound on the codimension of the complement of <math id="S5.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>). For arbitrary <math id="S5.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>, the coefficient of <math id="S5.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> in the bounds we obtain will be sharp (and the same for <math id="S5.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>).
In any particular case, however, one may find slight improvements on our bounds by enumerating the splitting loci in the complement <math id="S5.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, and calculating their codimensions.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Along the way, we also bound the codimension of the complement of <math id="S5.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{k,g}^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{k,g}^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math>. We point out some immediate corollaries regarding the Chow rings of <math id="S5.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{k,g}^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{k,g}^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math>, which will be used in our subsequent work <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.1. </span>Degree <math id="S5.SS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="S5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As a warm-up, we first explain our set-up in degree <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>, as it is simplest. The results in this subsection are not new (they have already been established by Bolognesi–Vistoli <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite> and Patel–Vakil <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>]</cite>) but spelling them out in our language will be instructive; it will also be useful in our subsequent work <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In Section <a href="#S4" title="4. Pairs of vector bundles on 
        
          
            
            P
            1
          
        
      -bundles ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, we gave a construction for <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{r,d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{r,d}</annotation></semantics></math> as the moduli space of vector bundles on <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-bundles.
As discussed in Section <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1. The category of triple covers ‣ 3. The Casnati–Ekedahl structure theorem ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, the linear algebraic data of a degree <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>, genus <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> cover involves a rank <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>, degree <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g+2</annotation></semantics></math> vector bundle <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and section of <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\det E^{\vee}\otimes\Sym^{3}E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Sym</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\det E^{\vee}\otimes\Sym^{3}E</annotation></semantics></math>. We set</p>
<table id="S5.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{3,g}:=\mathcal{V}_{2,g+2}\qquad\text{and}\qquad\mathcal{U}_{3,g}:=\det\mathcal{E}^{\vee}\otimes\Sym^{3}\mathcal{E}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Sym</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{3,g}:=\mathcal{V}_{2,g+2}\qquad\text{and}\qquad\mathcal{U}_{3,g}:=\det\mathcal{E}^{\vee}\otimes\Sym^{3}\mathcal{E},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math> is the universal rank <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> bundle on <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi:\mathcal{P}\to\mathcal{V}_{2,g+2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi:\mathcal{P}\to\mathcal{V}_{2,g+2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
There is a natural map <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{3,g}\to\mathcal{B}_{3,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{3,g}\to\mathcal{B}_{3,g}</annotation></semantics></math> that sends a family of triple covers <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\xrightarrow{\alpha}P\rightarrow S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝛼</mo></mover><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\xrightarrow{\alpha}P\rightarrow S</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{3,g}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{3,g}(S)</annotation></semantics></math> to the associated rank <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> vector bundle <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\to S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\to S</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{3,g}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{3,g}(S)</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\xrightarrow{\alpha}\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝛼</mo></mover><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\xrightarrow{\alpha}\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is an integral triple cover and
<math id="S5.SS1.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\alpha}=\mathcal{O}(e_{1})\oplus\mathcal{O}(e_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\alpha}=\mathcal{O}(e_{1})\oplus\mathcal{O}(e_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> is the associated rank <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> vector bundle on <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, then by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>, Proposition 2.2]</cite>, we have <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{1},e_{2}\geq\frac{g+2}{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{1},e_{2}\geq\frac{g+2}{3}</annotation></semantics></math>. Equivalently, every summand of <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\det E_{\alpha}^{\vee}\otimes\Sym^{3}E_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi><mo>∨</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Sym</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\det E_{\alpha}^{\vee}\otimes\Sym^{3}E_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> is non-negative. Hence, the map <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{3,g}\to\mathcal{B}_{3,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{3,g}\to\mathcal{B}_{3,g}</annotation></semantics></math> factors through the substack <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{3,g}^{\prime}\subseteq\mathcal{B}_{3,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{3,g}^{\prime}\subseteq\mathcal{B}_{3,g}</annotation></semantics></math> over which <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{3,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{3,g}</annotation></semantics></math> is globally generated on fibers of <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}\to\mathcal{B}_{3,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}\to\mathcal{B}_{3,g}</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{3,g}^{\prime}=\mathcal{H}_{3,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{3,g}^{\prime}=\mathcal{H}_{3,g}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We define <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{3,g}^{\prime}:=\pi_{*}\mathcal{U}_{3,g}|_{\mathcal{B}_{3,g}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{3,g}^{\prime}:=\pi_{*}\mathcal{U}_{3,g}|_{\mathcal{B}_{3,g}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is a vector bundle on <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{3,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{3,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> by the theorem on cohomology and base change.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmthm1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5.1</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There is an open inclusion <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{3,g}=\mathcal{H}_{3,g}^{\prime}\to\mathcal{X}_{3,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{3,g}=\mathcal{H}_{3,g}^{\prime}\to\mathcal{X}_{3,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\mathcal{H}_{3,g})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\mathcal{H}_{3,g})</annotation></semantics></math> is generated by the CE classes <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2},a_{1},a_{2},a_{2}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2},a_{1},a_{2},a_{2}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, and therefore <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\mathcal{H}_{3,g})=R^{*}(\mathcal{H}_{3,g})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\mathcal{H}_{3,g})=R^{*}(\mathcal{H}_{3,g})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">The first sentence was essentially observed in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>, p. 12]</cite>. We include an explanation using our notation.
Given a scheme <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, the objects of <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{3,g}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{3,g}(S)</annotation></semantics></math> are tuples <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(P\to S,E,\eta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(P\to S,E,\eta)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(P\to S,E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(P\to S,E)</annotation></semantics></math> is an object of <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{3,g}^{\prime}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{3,g}^{\prime}(S)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\in H^{0}(P,\Sym^{3}E\otimes\det E^{\vee})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Sym</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\in H^{0}(P,\Sym^{3}E\otimes\det E^{\vee})</annotation></semantics></math>. We define an open substack <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}_{3,g}^{\prime}\subset\mathcal{X}_{3,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>⊂</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}_{3,g}^{\prime}\subset\mathcal{X}_{3,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> by the condition that <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(\Phi(\eta))\subset\mathbb{P}E^{\vee}\to S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(\Phi(\eta))\subset\mathbb{P}E^{\vee}\to S</annotation></semantics></math> is a family of smooth curves, where <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> is as in (<a href="#S3.E6" title="In 3.1. The category of triple covers ‣ 3. The Casnati–Ekedahl structure theorem ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.6</span></a>). Considering the Hilbert polynomial of <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(\Phi(\eta))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(\Phi(\eta))</annotation></semantics></math>, one sees that the fibers have arithmetic genus <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>.
Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmthm4" title="Theorem 3.4 (Miranda, Casnati–Ekedahl). ‣ 3.1. The category of triple covers ‣ 3. The Casnati–Ekedahl structure theorem ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a> now shows that there is an equivalence <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{3,g}^{\prime}\cong\mathcal{Y}_{3,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≅</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{3,g}^{\prime}\cong\mathcal{Y}_{3,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">By excision, the Chow ring of <math id="S5.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{3,g}=\mathcal{H}_{3,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{3,g}=\mathcal{H}_{3,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is generated by restrictions of classes on <math id="S5.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{3,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{3,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S5.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{3,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{3,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is a vector bundle over <math id="S5.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{3,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{3,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, their Chow rings are isomorphic, so the statement about generators follows from Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmthm4" title="Theorem 4.4. ‣ 4.1. The rational Chow ring ‣ 4. Pairs of vector bundles on 
        
          
            
            P
            1
          
        
      -bundles ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.2. </span>Degree <math id="S5.SS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By Casnati–Ekedahl’s characterization of quadruple covers (Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmthm6" title="Theorem 3.6 (Casnati–Ekedahl). ‣ 3.2. The category of quadruple covers ‣ 3. The Casnati–Ekedahl structure theorem ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.6</span></a>), the linear algebraic data of a quadruple cover of <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is equivalent to the data of: a rank <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> vector bundle <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>; a rank <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> vector bundle <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>; an isomorphism <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\det F\cong\det E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≅</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\det F\cong\det E</annotation></semantics></math>; and a global section of <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F^{\vee}\otimes\Sym^{2}E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Sym</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F^{\vee}\otimes\Sym^{2}E</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> having the right codimension. By Example <a href="#S3.Thmthm1" title="Example 3.1 (Covers of 
          
            
              
              P
              1
            
          
        ). ‣ 3. The Casnati–Ekedahl structure theorem ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg(E)=\deg(F)=g+3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg(E)=\deg(F)=g+3</annotation></semantics></math>.
The stacks <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{2,g+3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{2,g+3}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{3,g+3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{3,g+3}</annotation></semantics></math> both admit natural morphisms to <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\BSL_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>BSL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\BSL_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the fiber product <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{3,g+3}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{2,g+3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>BSL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{3,g+3}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{2,g+3}</annotation></semantics></math> is the stack whose objects are quadruples <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(S,V,E,F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S,V,E,F)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-scheme, <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> is a rank <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>-vector bundle with trivial determinant, <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> is a rank <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> vector bundle on <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}V</annotation></semantics></math> whose restriction to the fibers of <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}V\rightarrow S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}V\rightarrow S</annotation></semantics></math> is globally generated of degree <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g+3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g+3</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> is a rank <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> vector bundle on <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}V</annotation></semantics></math> whose restriction to the fibers of <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}V\rightarrow S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}V\rightarrow S</annotation></semantics></math> is globally generated of degree <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g+3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g+3</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The additional data of an isomorphism <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\det F\cong\det E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≅</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\det F\cong\det E</annotation></semantics></math> is captured by a <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{G}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔾</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{G}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> torsor over <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{3,g+3}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{2,g+3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>BSL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{3,g+3}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{2,g+3}</annotation></semantics></math> defined as follows.
Let <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math> be the universal rank <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> bundle and <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> be the universal rank <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> bundle on the universal <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-bundle <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi:\mathcal{P}\rightarrow\mathcal{V}_{3,g+3}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{2,g+3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>BSL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi:\mathcal{P}\rightarrow\mathcal{V}_{3,g+3}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{2,g+3}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\det\mathcal{E}^{\vee}\otimes\det\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\det\mathcal{E}^{\vee}\otimes\det\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> has degree <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> on each fiber of <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi:\mathcal{P}\rightarrow\mathcal{V}_{3,g+3}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{2,g+3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>BSL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi:\mathcal{P}\rightarrow\mathcal{V}_{3,g+3}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{2,g+3}</annotation></semantics></math>, the theorem on cohomology and base change shows that
<math id="S5.SS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}:=\pi_{*}(\det\mathcal{E}^{\vee}\otimes\det\mathcal{F})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}:=\pi_{*}(\det\mathcal{E}^{\vee}\otimes\det\mathcal{F})</annotation></semantics></math>
is a line bundle with <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}\mathcal{L}\cong\det\mathcal{E}^{\vee}\otimes\det\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≅</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}\mathcal{L}\cong\det\mathcal{E}^{\vee}\otimes\det\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmthm2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 5.2</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmthm2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">With notation as above, define the stack <math id="S5.Thmthm2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{4,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{4,g}</annotation></semantics></math> to be the <math id="S5.Thmthm2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{G}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔾</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{G}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>-torsor over <math id="S5.Thmthm2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{3,g+3}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{2,g+3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>BSL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{3,g+3}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{2,g+3}</annotation></semantics></math> given by the complement of the zero section of the line bundle <math id="S5.Thmthm2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The objects of <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{4,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{4,g}</annotation></semantics></math> are tuples <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(S,V,E,F,\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S,V,E,F,\phi)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(S,V,E,F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S,V,E,F)</annotation></semantics></math> is an object of <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{3,g+3}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{2,g+3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>BSL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{3,g+3}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{2,g+3}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> is an isomorphism <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\det F\cong\det E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≅</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\det F\cong\det E</annotation></semantics></math>.
Recalling the notation of Section <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2. The category of quadruple covers ‣ 3. The Casnati–Ekedahl structure theorem ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>, given an object <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\xrightarrow{\alpha}P\to S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝛼</mo></mover><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\xrightarrow{\alpha}P\to S</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{4,g}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{4,g}(S)</annotation></semantics></math>, the restriction of <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> to fibers of <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\to S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\to S</annotation></semantics></math> are both known to be globally generated (see Proposition <a href="#S5.Thmthm6" title="Proposition 5.6. ‣ 5.2. Degree 
          
            4 ‣ 5. The good opens and codimension bounds ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.6</span></a>).
Hence,
there is a natural map <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{4,g}\to\mathcal{B}_{4,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{4,g}\to\mathcal{B}_{4,g}</annotation></semantics></math> that sends the family <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\xrightarrow{\alpha}P\xrightarrow{\pi}S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝛼</mo></mover><mi>P</mi><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝜋</mo></mover><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\xrightarrow{\alpha}P\xrightarrow{\pi}S</annotation></semantics></math> to the tuple <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(S,\pi_{*}\mathcal{O}_{P}(1)^{\vee},E_{\alpha},F_{\alpha},\phi_{\alpha})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S,\pi_{*}\mathcal{O}_{P}(1)^{\vee},E_{\alpha},F_{\alpha},\phi_{\alpha})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">By slight abuse of notation, let us denote the pullback to <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{4,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{4,g}</annotation></semantics></math> of the universal <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-bundle by <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi:\mathcal{P}\rightarrow\mathcal{B}_{4,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi:\mathcal{P}\rightarrow\mathcal{B}_{4,g}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the universal rank <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> vector bundles on it by <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=\mathcal{O}_{\mathcal{P}}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=\mathcal{O}_{\mathcal{P}}(1)</annotation></semantics></math> and write</p>
<table id="S5.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}(\mathcal{E})=\pi^{*}a_{i}+(\pi^{*}a_{i}^{\prime})z\qquad\text{and}\qquad c_{i}(\mathcal{F})=\pi^{*}b_{i}+(\pi^{*}b_{i}^{\prime})z." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}(\mathcal{E})=\pi^{*}a_{i}+(\pi^{*}a_{i}^{\prime})z\qquad\text{and}\qquad c_{i}(\mathcal{F})=\pi^{*}b_{i}+(\pi^{*}b_{i}^{\prime})z.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">for <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i},b_{i}\in A^{i}(\mathcal{B}_{4,g})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i},b_{i}\in A^{i}(\mathcal{B}_{4,g})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}^{\prime},b_{i}^{\prime}\in A^{i-1}(\mathcal{B}_{4,g})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}^{\prime},b_{i}^{\prime}\in A^{i-1}(\mathcal{B}_{4,g})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Note that <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1}^{\prime}=b_{1}^{\prime}=g+3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1}^{\prime}=b_{1}^{\prime}=g+3</annotation></semantics></math>.
Moreover, by definition of <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{4,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{4,g}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}(\det\mathcal{E}^{\vee}\otimes\det\mathcal{F})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}(\det\mathcal{E}^{\vee}\otimes\det\mathcal{F})=0</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1}=b_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1}=b_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Further, by Lemma <a href="#S2.Thmthm1" title="Lemma 2.1. ‣ 2.2. (Equivariant) Intersection Theory ‣ 2. Notation and conventions ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>, we have</p>
<table id="S5.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(5.4)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A^{*}(\mathcal{B}_{4,g})=A^{*}(\mathcal{V}_{3,g+3}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{2,g+3})/\langle c_{1}(\mathcal{L})\rangle=A^{*}(\mathcal{V}_{3,g+3}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{2,g+3})/\langle a_{1}-b_{1}\rangle." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>BSL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>BSL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A^{*}(\mathcal{B}_{4,g})=A^{*}(\mathcal{V}_{3,g+3}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{2,g+3})/\langle c_{1}(\mathcal{L})\rangle=A^{*}(\mathcal{V}_{3,g+3}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{2,g+3})/\langle a_{1}-b_{1}\rangle.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p4.3" class="ltx_p">Thus, Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmthm4" title="Theorem 4.4. ‣ 4.1. The rational Chow ring ‣ 4. Pairs of vector bundles on 
        
          
            
            P
            1
          
        
      -bundles ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a>
shows that <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2},a_{1},a_{2},a_{3},a_{2}^{\prime},a_{3}^{\prime},b_{2}^{\prime},b_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2},a_{1},a_{2},a_{3},a_{2}^{\prime},a_{3}^{\prime},b_{2}^{\prime},b_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> generate <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\mathcal{B}_{4,g})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\mathcal{B}_{4,g})</annotation></semantics></math> and</p>
<table id="S5.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(5.5)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\trun^{g+4}A^{*}(\mathcal{B}_{4,g})=\trun^{g+4}\mathbb{Q}[c_{2},a_{1},a_{2},a_{3},a_{2}^{\prime},a_{3}^{\prime},b_{2}^{\prime},b_{2}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Trun</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Trun</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\trun^{g+4}A^{*}(\mathcal{B}_{4,g})=\trun^{g+4}\mathbb{Q}[c_{2},a_{1},a_{2},a_{3},a_{2}^{\prime},a_{3}^{\prime},b_{2}^{\prime},b_{2}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we define <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{4,g}:=\mathcal{F}^{\vee}\otimes\Sym^{2}\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Sym</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{4,g}:=\mathcal{F}^{\vee}\otimes\Sym^{2}\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math>. We then define <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{4,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{4,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{4,g}^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{4,g}^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math> by (<a href="#S5.E1" title="In 5. The good opens and codimension bounds ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>) and (<a href="#S5.E2" title="In 5. The good opens and codimension bounds ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>) respectively.
Correspondingly, the open substacks <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\circ}\subseteq\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\prime}\subseteq\mathcal{H}_{4,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo>⊆</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\circ}\subseteq\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\prime}\subseteq\mathcal{H}_{4,g}</annotation></semantics></math> are described by</p>
<table id="S5.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\{S\rightarrow\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\circ}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\{S\rightarrow\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\circ}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\{S\rightarrow\mathcal{H}_{4,g}:R^{1}(\pi_{S})_{*}(\mathcal{F}_{S}^{\vee}\otimes\Sym^{2}\mathcal{E}_{S}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{\mathcal{P}_{S}}(-2))=0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>∨</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Sym</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\{S\rightarrow\mathcal{H}_{4,g}:R^{1}(\pi_{S})_{*}(\mathcal{F}_{S}^{\vee}\otimes\Sym^{2}\mathcal{E}_{S}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{\mathcal{P}_{S}}(-2))=0\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\{S\rightarrow\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\prime}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\{S\rightarrow\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\prime}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\{S\rightarrow\mathcal{H}_{4,g}:R^{1}(\pi_{S})_{*}(\mathcal{F}_{S}^{\vee}\otimes\Sym^{2}\mathcal{E}_{S})=0\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>∨</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Sym</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\{S\rightarrow\mathcal{H}_{4,g}:R^{1}(\pi_{S})_{*}(\mathcal{F}_{S}^{\vee}\otimes\Sym^{2}\mathcal{E}_{S})=0\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">The key property of <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is that the map <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\prime}\to\mathcal{B}_{4,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\prime}\to\mathcal{B}_{4,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> factors through an open inclusion in the total space of a vector bundle <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{4,g}^{\prime}:=\pi_{*}\mathcal{U}_{4,g}|_{\mathcal{B}_{4,g}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{4,g}^{\prime}:=\pi_{*}\mathcal{U}_{4,g}|_{\mathcal{B}_{4,g}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmthm3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5.3</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmthm3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There is an open inclusion <math id="S5.Thmthm3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\prime}\to\mathcal{X}_{4,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\prime}\to\mathcal{X}_{4,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, <math id="S5.Thmthm3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\prime})=R^{*}(\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\prime})=R^{*}(\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> is generated by the CE classes <math id="S5.Thmthm3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2},a_{1},a_{2},a_{3},a_{2}^{\prime},a_{3}^{\prime},b_{2}^{\prime},b_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2},a_{1},a_{2},a_{3},a_{2}^{\prime},a_{3}^{\prime},b_{2}^{\prime},b_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">The objects of <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{4,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{4,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> are tuples <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(S,V,E,F,\phi,\eta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S,V,E,F,\phi,\eta)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(S,V,E,F,\phi)\in\mathcal{B}_{4,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S,V,E,F,\phi)\in\mathcal{B}_{4,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\in H^{0}(\mathbb{P}V,F^{\vee}\otimes\Sym^{2}E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Sym</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\in H^{0}(\mathbb{P}V,F^{\vee}\otimes\Sym^{2}E)</annotation></semantics></math>. Letting <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> be as in (<a href="#S3.E9" title="In 3.2. The category of quadruple covers ‣ 3. The Casnati–Ekedahl structure theorem ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.9</span></a>), we define <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}_{4,g}\subset\mathcal{X}_{4,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}_{4,g}\subset\mathcal{X}_{4,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> to be the open substack defined by the condition that <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(\Phi(\eta))\subset\mathbb{P}E^{\vee}\to S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(\Phi(\eta))\subset\mathbb{P}E^{\vee}\to S</annotation></semantics></math> is a family of smooth curves. Considering the Hilbert polynomial of <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(\Phi(\eta))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(\Phi(\eta))</annotation></semantics></math>, using (<a href="#S3.E7" title="In 3.2. The category of quadruple covers ‣ 3. The Casnati–Ekedahl structure theorem ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.7</span></a>), we see that the fibers have arithmetic genus <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>.
Using Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmthm6" title="Theorem 3.6 (Casnati–Ekedahl). ‣ 3.2. The category of quadruple covers ‣ 3. The Casnati–Ekedahl structure theorem ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.6</span></a>, we see that <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is equivalent to <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}_{4,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}_{4,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">By excision, the Chow ring of <math id="S5.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is generated by restriction of classes from <math id="S5.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{4,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{4,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S5.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{4,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{4,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is a vector bundle over <math id="S5.SS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{4,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{4,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, their Chow rings are isomorphic, so the statement about generators follows from (<a href="#S5.E4" title="In 5.2. Degree 
          
            4 ‣ 5. The good opens and codimension bounds ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.4</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmthm4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5.4</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The codimension of <math id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Supp(R^{1}\pi_{*}(\mathcal{U}_{4,g}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{\mathcal{P}}(-2)))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Supp(R^{1}\pi_{*}(\mathcal{U}_{4,g}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{\mathcal{P}}(-2)))</annotation></semantics></math> is at least <math id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{g+3}{4}-4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{g+3}{4}-4</annotation></semantics></math>. That is, the codimension of the complement of <math id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{4,g}^{\circ}\subseteq\mathcal{B}_{4,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{4,g}^{\circ}\subseteq\mathcal{B}_{4,g}</annotation></semantics></math> has codimension at least <math id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{g+3}{4}-4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{g+3}{4}-4</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">By equation (<a href="#S4.E7" title="In 4.2. Splitting loci ‣ 4. Pairs of vector bundles on 
        
          
            
            P
            1
          
        
      -bundles ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.7</span></a>),
the codimension of the support of <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{1}\pi_{*}(\mathcal{F}^{\vee}\otimes\Sym^{2}\mathcal{E}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{\mathcal{P}}(-2))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Sym</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{1}\pi_{*}(\mathcal{F}^{\vee}\otimes\Sym^{2}\mathcal{E}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{\mathcal{P}}(-2))</annotation></semantics></math> is the minimum value of
<math id="S5.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{E}nd(\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})))+h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{E}nd(\mathcal{O}(\vec{f}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{E}nd(\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})))+h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{E}nd(\mathcal{O}(\vec{f}))</annotation></semantics></math>
as we range over splitting types <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{e}=(e_{1},e_{2},e_{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{e}=(e_{1},e_{2},e_{3})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{1}\leq e_{2}\leq e_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{1}\leq e_{2}\leq e_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{f}=(f_{1},f_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{f}=(f_{1},f_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{1}\leq f_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{1}\leq f_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})^{\vee}\otimes(\Sym^{2}\mathcal{O}(\vec{e}))\otimes\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{1}}(-2))&gt;0\qquad\Leftrightarrow\qquad 2e_{1}\leq f_{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∨</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>Sym</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})^{\vee}\otimes(\Sym^{2}\mathcal{O}(\vec{e}))\otimes\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{1}}(-2))&gt;0\qquad\Leftrightarrow\qquad 2e_{1}\leq f_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">We have</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{E}nd(\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})))+h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{E}nd(\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})))\geq 2e_{3}-2e_{1}-3+f_{2}-f_{1}-1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{E}nd(\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})))+h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{E}nd(\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})))\geq 2e_{3}-2e_{1}-3+f_{2}-f_{1}-1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">To find the minimum, we consider the function of <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> real variables</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x_{1},x_{2},x_{3},y_{1},y_{2}):=2x_{3}-2x_{1}+y_{2}-y_{1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x_{1},x_{2},x_{3},y_{1},y_{2}):=2x_{3}-2x_{1}+y_{2}-y_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p8.4.1" class="ltx_text">on the compact region <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> defined by</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 0\leq x_{1}\leq x_{2}\leq x_{3},\quad x_{1}+x_{2}+x_{3}=1,\quad y_{1}\leq y_{2},\quad y_{1}+y_{2}=1,\quad 2x_{1}\leq y_{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 0\leq x_{1}\leq x_{2}\leq x_{3},\quad x_{1}+x_{2}+x_{3}=1,\quad y_{1}\leq y_{2},\quad y_{1}+y_{2}=1,\quad 2x_{1}\leq y_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p8.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p8.5.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is piecewise linear, its extreme values are attained where multiple boundary conditions intersect at a point. Code provided at <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite> performs the linear algebra to locate such points and evaluates <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> at the them to determine its minimum. The minimum is <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{4}</annotation></semantics></math>, attained at <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\frac{1}{4},\frac{3}{8},\frac{3}{8},\frac{1}{2},\frac{1}{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\frac{1}{4},\frac{3}{8},\frac{3}{8},\frac{1}{2},\frac{1}{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus,</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim\Supp R^{1}\pi_{*}(\mathcal{U}_{4,g}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{\mathcal{P}}(-2))\geq(g+3)\cdot\min_{D}(f)-4=\frac{g+3}{4}-4.\qed" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">dim</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Supp</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>D</mi></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" lspace="0.0835em" mathvariant="italic" separator="true">∎</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim\Supp R^{1}\pi_{*}(\mathcal{U}_{4,g}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{\mathcal{P}}(-2))\geq(g+3)\cdot\min_{D}(f)-4=\frac{g+3}{4}-4.\qed</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p">For later use, let us note an immediate consequence of the previous lemma: Using excision and (<a href="#S5.Thmthm4" title="Lemma 5.4. ‣ 5.2. Degree 
          
            4 ‣ 5. The good opens and codimension bounds ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.4</span></a>), we see</p>
<table id="S5.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(5.6)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\trun^{(g+3)/4-4}A^{*}(\mathcal{B}_{4,g}^{\circ})=\trun^{(g+3)/4-4}\mathbb{Q}[c_{2},a_{1},a_{2},a_{3},a_{2}^{\prime},a_{3}^{\prime},b_{2}^{\prime},b_{2}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Trun</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Trun</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\trun^{(g+3)/4-4}A^{*}(\mathcal{B}_{4,g}^{\circ})=\trun^{(g+3)/4-4}\mathbb{Q}[c_{2},a_{1},a_{2},a_{3},a_{2}^{\prime},a_{3}^{\prime},b_{2}^{\prime},b_{2}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p">Just because the complement of <math id="S5.SS2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{4,g}^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{4,g}^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math> has high codimension inside <math id="S5.SS2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{4,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{4,g}</annotation></semantics></math> does <span id="S5.SS2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">not</span> mean that the complement of <math id="S5.SS2.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math> will have high codimension in <math id="S5.SS2.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{4,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{4,g}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The condition for <math id="S5.SS2.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha:C\to\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha:C\to\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> to be in <math id="S5.SS2.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math> is that <math id="S5.SS2.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},F_{\alpha}^{\vee}\otimes\Sym^{2}E_{\alpha})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi><mo>∨</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Sym</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},F_{\alpha}^{\vee}\otimes\Sym^{2}E_{\alpha})=0</annotation></semantics></math>. We shall refer to this as “our cohomological condition.” Our cohomological condition fails for factoring covers, as we explain now.
Suppose <math id="S5.SS2.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha:C\rightarrow\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha:C\rightarrow\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> factors as <math id="S5.SS2.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\xrightarrow{\beta}C^{\prime}\xrightarrow{h}\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝛽</mo></mover><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">ℎ</mo></mover><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\xrightarrow{\beta}C^{\prime}\xrightarrow{h}\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S5.SS2.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> has genus <math id="S5.SS2.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. We claim <math id="S5.SS2.p10.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\alpha}=\mathcal{O}(g^{\prime}+1)\oplus E^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\alpha}=\mathcal{O}(g^{\prime}+1)\oplus E^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> for some rank <math id="S5.SS2.p10.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> bundle <math id="S5.SS2.p10.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Indeed, because <math id="S5.SS2.p10.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> is a double cover, we have</p>
<table id="S5.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{*}\mathcal{O}_{C}\cong\mathcal{O}_{C^{\prime}}\oplus L," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>⊕</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{*}\mathcal{O}_{C}\cong\mathcal{O}_{C^{\prime}}\oplus L,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p10.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S5.SS2.p10.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> is a line bundle on <math id="S5.SS2.p10.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Pushing forward again by <math id="S5.SS2.p10.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S5.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{*}\mathcal{O}_{C}\cong\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{1}}\oplus\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{1}}(-g^{\prime}-1)\oplus h_{*}L." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{*}\mathcal{O}_{C}\cong\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{1}}\oplus\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{1}}(-g^{\prime}-1)\oplus h_{*}L.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p10.3" class="ltx_p">This establishes that <math id="S5.SS2.p10.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> has an <math id="S5.SS2.p10.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(g^{\prime}+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(g^{\prime}+1)</annotation></semantics></math> summand. In particular, since some summand of <math id="S5.SS2.p10.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> has degree at least <math id="S5.SS2.p10.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{g+3}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{g+3}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S5.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},F^{\vee}\otimes\Sym^{2}E)\geq\frac{g+3}{2}-2(g^{\prime}+1)-1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Sym</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},F^{\vee}\otimes\Sym^{2}E)\geq\frac{g+3}{2}-2(g^{\prime}+1)-1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p10.4" class="ltx_p">Thus, covers that factor with <math id="S5.SS2.p10.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> small are never in <math id="S5.SS2.p10.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}^{\circ}_{4,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}^{\circ}_{4,g}</annotation></semantics></math>.
More precisely, if a factoring cover does satisfy our cohomological condition, then the genus of the intermediate curve must satisfy <math id="S5.SS2.p10.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2(g^{\prime}+1)\geq\frac{g+3}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2(g^{\prime}+1)\geq\frac{g+3}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmthm5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5.5</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmthm5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The locus of degree <math id="S5.Thmthm5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> covers <math id="S5.Thmthm5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\to\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\to\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> that factor <math id="S5.Thmthm5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\rightarrow C^{\prime}\rightarrow\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\rightarrow C^{\prime}\rightarrow\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S5.Thmthm5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> has genus <math id="S5.Thmthm5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> has codimension <math id="S5.Thmthm5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2(g^{\prime}+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2(g^{\prime}+1)</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S5.Thmthm5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{4,g}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{4,g}.</annotation></semantics></math> Hence, the complement of <math id="S5.Thmthm5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}^{\circ}_{4,g}\cap\mathcal{H}^{\mathrm{nf}}_{4,g}\subset\mathcal{H}^{\circ}_{4,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo>∩</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>nf</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}^{\circ}_{4,g}\cap\mathcal{H}^{\mathrm{nf}}_{4,g}\subset\mathcal{H}^{\circ}_{4,g}</annotation></semantics></math> has codimension at least <math id="S5.Thmthm5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{g+3}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{g+3}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">The dimension of the Hurwitz stack is the degree of the branch locus minus <math id="S5.SS2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3=\dim\Aut(\mathbb{P}^{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">dim</mo><mrow><mi>Aut</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3=\dim\Aut(\mathbb{P}^{1})</annotation></semantics></math>, giving <math id="S5.SS2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim\mathcal{H}_{4,g}=2g+3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">dim</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim\mathcal{H}_{4,g}=2g+3</annotation></semantics></math>. Meanwhile, by Riemann–Hurwitz, the dimension of the space of genus <math id="S5.SS2.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> double covers of a fixed curve <math id="S5.SS2.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> of genus <math id="S5.SS2.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S5.SS2.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2g-2-2(2g^{\prime}-2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2g-2-2(2g^{\prime}-2)</annotation></semantics></math>. The dimension of the stack of genus <math id="S5.SS2.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> double covers of <math id="S5.SS2.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> modulo <math id="S5.SS2.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Aut(\mathbb{P}^{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Aut</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Aut(\mathbb{P}^{1})</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S5.SS2.p11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2g^{\prime}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2g^{\prime}-1</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, the dimension of the space of degree <math id="S5.SS2.p11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> covers that factor through a curve of genus <math id="S5.SS2.p11.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2g-2-2(2g^{\prime}-2)+2g^{\prime}-1=2g+1-2g^{\prime}=\dim\mathcal{H}_{4,g}-2(g^{\prime}+1).\qed" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">dim</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" lspace="0.0835em" mathvariant="italic" separator="true">∎</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2g-2-2(2g^{\prime}-2)+2g^{\prime}-1=2g+1-2g^{\prime}=\dim\mathcal{H}_{4,g}-2(g^{\prime}+1).\qed</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p12.1" class="ltx_p">Covers that factor through a curve of low <math id="S5.SS2.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> are therefore loci of fixed codimension that fail our cohomological condition. For this reason, in degree <math id="S5.SS2.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math>, our techniques will only prove that certain Chow groups of the locus of <span id="S5.SS2.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">non-factoring</span> covers are generated by tautological classes.
Below, we collect some results about the splitting types of the vector bundles associated to a degree <math id="S5.SS2.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> cover. These facts were known to Schreyer <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>]</cite> (though Schreyer’s notation differs from ours). We include proofs here as they demonstrate the geometric meaning of splitting types.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmthm6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 5.6</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmthm6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose <math id="S5.Thmthm6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha:C\rightarrow\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha:C\rightarrow\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is a degree <math id="S5.Thmthm6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> cover and <math id="S5.Thmthm6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\alpha}=\mathcal{O}(e_{1})\oplus\mathcal{O}(e_{2})\oplus\mathcal{O}(e_{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\alpha}=\mathcal{O}(e_{1})\oplus\mathcal{O}(e_{2})\oplus\mathcal{O}(e_{3})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S5.Thmthm6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{1}\leq e_{2}\leq e_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{1}\leq e_{2}\leq e_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S5.Thmthm6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=\mathcal{O}(f_{1})\oplus\mathcal{O}(f_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=\mathcal{O}(f_{1})\oplus\mathcal{O}(f_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S5.Thmthm6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{1}\leq f_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{1}\leq f_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. The following are true:</span></p>
<ol id="S5.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{1}+e_{2}+e_{3}=f_{1}+f_{2}=g+3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{1}+e_{2}+e_{3}=f_{1}+f_{2}=g+3</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and with </span><math id="S5.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{1}\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{1}\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> if </span><math id="S5.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> irreducible.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If </span><math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is irreducible, </span><math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2e_{1}\geq f_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2e_{1}\geq f_{1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, and </span><math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2e_{2}\geq f_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2e_{2}\geq f_{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I1.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Hence </span><math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I1.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is globally generated.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If </span><math id="S5.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> does not factor then </span><math id="S5.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{1}+e_{3}-f_{2}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{1}+e_{3}-f_{2}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I1.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS2.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">(1) follows from Example <a href="#S3.Thmthm1" title="Example 3.1 (Covers of 
          
            
              
              P
              1
            
          
        ). ‣ 3. The Casnati–Ekedahl structure theorem ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> and fact that <math id="S5.SS2.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\det E_{\alpha}\cong\det F_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≅</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\det E_{\alpha}\cong\det F_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S5.SS2.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is irreducible, we have <math id="S5.SS2.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{0}(\mathbb{P}^{1},E_{\alpha}^{\vee})=h^{0}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\alpha_{*}\mathcal{O}_{C})-1=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi><mo>∨</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{0}(\mathbb{P}^{1},E_{\alpha}^{\vee})=h^{0}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\alpha_{*}\mathcal{O}_{C})-1=0</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="S5.SS2.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{1}\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{1}\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">The remaining conditions can be seen from the description of <math id="S5.SS2.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> as the intersection of two relative quadrics on <math id="S5.SS2.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}E_{\alpha}^{\vee}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi><mo>∨</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}E_{\alpha}^{\vee}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let us choose a splitting <math id="S5.SS2.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E=\mathcal{O}(e_{1})\oplus\mathcal{O}(e_{2})\oplus\mathcal{O}(e_{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E=\mathcal{O}(e_{1})\oplus\mathcal{O}(e_{2})\oplus\mathcal{O}(e_{3})</annotation></semantics></math> and corresponding coordinates <math id="S5.SS2.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X,Y,Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X,Y,Z</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S5.SS2.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}E^{\vee}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}E^{\vee}</annotation></semantics></math>. The two quadrics that define <math id="S5.SS2.p14.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> are of the form</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(5.7)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=p_{1,1}X^{2}+p_{1,2}XY+p_{2,2}Y^{2}+p_{1,3}XZ+p_{2,3}YZ+p_{3,3}Z^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=p_{1,1}X^{2}+p_{1,2}XY+p_{2,2}Y^{2}+p_{1,3}XZ+p_{2,3}YZ+p_{3,3}Z^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(5.8)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=q_{1,1}X^{2}+q_{1,2}XY+q_{2,2}Y^{2}+q_{1,3}XZ+q_{2,3}YZ+q_{3,3},Z^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=q_{1,1}X^{2}+q_{1,2}XY+q_{2,2}Y^{2}+q_{1,3}XZ+q_{2,3}YZ+q_{3,3},Z^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p14.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p14.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S5.SS2.p14.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> is a polynomial on <math id="S5.SS2.p14.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> of degree <math id="S5.SS2.p14.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{i}+e_{j}-f_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{i}+e_{j}-f_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p14.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> is a polynomial on <math id="S5.SS2.p14.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> of degree <math id="S5.SS2.p14.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{i}+e_{j}-f_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{i}+e_{j}-f_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. If this degree is negative, then we mean this coefficient is zero.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">(2) If <math id="S5.SS2.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2e_{1}&lt;f_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2e_{1}&lt;f_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S5.SS2.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1,1}=q_{1,1}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1,1}=q_{1,1}=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=V(p,q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=V(p,q)</annotation></semantics></math> would contain the curve <math id="S5.SS2.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=Z=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=Z=0</annotation></semantics></math>, forcing <math id="S5.SS2.p15.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> to be reducible. If <math id="S5.SS2.p15.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2e_{2}&lt;f_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2e_{2}&lt;f_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S5.SS2.p15.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{1,1}=q_{1,2}=q_{2,2}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{1,1}=q_{1,2}=q_{2,2}=0</annotation></semantics></math> so <math id="S5.SS2.p15.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> divides <math id="S5.SS2.p15.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S5.SS2.p15.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> were irreducible, it would be contained in one of the linear components of <math id="S5.SS2.p15.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(q)</annotation></semantics></math> but this is impossible. The global generation of <math id="S5.SS2.p15.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> follows because the inequalities imply <math id="S5.SS2.p15.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{1}=g+3-f_{2}\geq e_{1}\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{1}=g+3-f_{2}\geq e_{1}\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">(3) If <math id="S5.SS2.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{1}+e_{3}-f_{2}\leq-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0em">≤</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{1}+e_{3}-f_{2}\leq-1</annotation></semantics></math>, then we show <math id="S5.SS2.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> factors. This inequality implies</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2e_{1}-f_{2}\leq e_{1}+e_{2}-f_{2}\leq e_{1}+e_{3}-f_{2}\leq-1," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0em">≤</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2e_{1}-f_{2}\leq e_{1}+e_{2}-f_{2}\leq e_{1}+e_{3}-f_{2}\leq-1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p16.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p16.2.1" class="ltx_text">so the coefficients <math id="S5.SS2.p16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1,1},p_{1,2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1,1},p_{1,2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S5.SS2.p16.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1,3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1,3}</annotation></semantics></math> vanish. Therefore, <math id="S5.SS2.p16.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> is a combination of <math id="S5.SS2.p16.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y^{2},YZ," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y^{2},YZ,</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p16.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, <math id="S5.SS2.p16.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(p)</annotation></semantics></math> is reducible in every fiber and contains the point <math id="S5.SS2.p16.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[1,0,0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[1,0,0]</annotation></semantics></math> in each fiber.</span></p><object type="image/svg+xml" data="/html/2103.09902/assets/factoring.svg" id="S5.SS2.p16.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" width="299" height="287"></object>
<p id="S5.SS2.p16.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p16.3.1" class="ltx_text">In other words, each fiber of <math id="S5.SS2.p16.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\to\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\to\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> consists of two pairs of points colinear with <math id="S5.SS2.p16.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[1,0,0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[1,0,0]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Projection away from the line <math id="S5.SS2.p16.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=Z=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=Z=0</annotation></semantics></math> defines a double cover <math id="S5.SS2.p16.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\to C^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\to C^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> that factors <math id="S5.SS2.p16.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p17.1" class="ltx_p">The simultaneous splitting loci of the universal <math id="S5.SS2.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S5.SS2.p17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{4,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{4,g}</annotation></semantics></math> give rise to a stratification of <math id="S5.SS2.p17.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{4,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{4,g}</annotation></semantics></math>.
In <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>, Remark 4.2]</cite>, Deopurkar–Patel show that the codimension of the splitting locus where <math id="S5.SS2.p17.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math> has splitting type <math id="S5.SS2.p17.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{e}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p17.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> has splitting type <math id="S5.SS2.p17.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{f}</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="S5.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(5.9)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{E}nd(\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})))+h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{E}nd(\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})))-h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})^{\vee}\otimes\Sym^{2}\mathcal{O}(\vec{e}))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Sym</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{E}nd(\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})))+h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{E}nd(\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})))-h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})^{\vee}\otimes\Sym^{2}\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p17.2" class="ltx_p">Note that this differs from (<a href="#S4.E7" title="In 4.2. Splitting loci ‣ 4. Pairs of vector bundles on 
        
          
            
            P
            1
          
        
      -bundles ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.7</span></a>) by <math id="S5.SS2.p17.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})^{\vee}\otimes\Sym^{2}\mathcal{O}(\vec{e}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Sym</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})^{\vee}\otimes\Sym^{2}\mathcal{O}(\vec{e}))</annotation></semantics></math>!</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmthm7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example 5.7</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<math id="S5.Thmthm7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=6</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="S5.Thmthm7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmthm7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We have <math id="S5.Thmthm7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim\mathcal{H}_{4,6}=\dim\mathcal{M}_{6}=15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">dim</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">dim</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim\mathcal{H}_{4,6}=\dim\mathcal{M}_{6}=15</annotation></semantics></math>.
Using Proposition <a href="#S5.Thmthm6" title="Proposition 5.6. ‣ 5.2. Degree 
          
            4 ‣ 5. The good opens and codimension bounds ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.6</span></a> (2), we see that the non-empty strata are</p>
<ol id="S5.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S5.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S5.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{e}=(3,3,3),\vec{f}=(4,5)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{e}=(3,3,3),\vec{f}=(4,5)</annotation></semantics></math>, (codimension <math id="S5.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>): The generic stratum.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S5.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{e}=(2,3,4),\vec{f}=(4,5)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{e}=(2,3,4),\vec{f}=(4,5)</annotation></semantics></math>, (codimension <math id="S5.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>): By Casnati-Del Centina <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite>, the bielliptic locus is contained in this stratum as the locus where <math id="S5.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1,2}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1,2}=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.I2.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1,3}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1,3}=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that <math id="S5.I2.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg(p_{1,2})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg(p_{1,2})=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.I2.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg(p_{1,3})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg(p_{1,3})=1</annotation></semantics></math>, so this represents <math id="S5.I2.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> conditions, making the bielliptic locus codimension <math id="S5.I2.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> inside <math id="S5.I2.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{4,6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{4,6}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S5.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{e}=(3,3,3),\vec{f}=(3,6)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{e}=(3,3,3),\vec{f}=(3,6)</annotation></semantics></math>, (codimension <math id="S5.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>): This stratum consists of trigonal curves. We have <math id="S5.I2.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}E^{\vee}\cong\mathbb{P}^{1}\times\mathbb{P}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}E^{\vee}\cong\mathbb{P}^{1}\times\mathbb{P}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S5.I2.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg(q_{i,j})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg(q_{i,j})=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.I2.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg(p_{i,j})=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg(p_{i,j})=3</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S5.I2.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j</annotation></semantics></math>, the projection onto the <math id="S5.I2.i3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> factor realizes <math id="S5.I2.i3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> as a degree <math id="S5.I2.i3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> cover of a conic in <math id="S5.I2.i3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4)</span> 
<div id="S5.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I2.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{e}=(2,3,4),\vec{f}=(3,6)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{e}=(2,3,4),\vec{f}=(3,6)</annotation></semantics></math>, (codimension 2): Curves with a <math id="S5.I2.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{2}_{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{2}_{5}</annotation></semantics></math>. We have <math id="S5.I2.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1,1}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1,1}=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.I2.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg(q_{1,1})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg(q_{1,1})=1</annotation></semantics></math>, so the curve meets the line <math id="S5.I2.i4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=Z=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=Z=0</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S5.I2.i4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}E^{\vee}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}E^{\vee}</annotation></semantics></math> in one point, say <math id="S5.I2.i4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu\in C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu\in C</annotation></semantics></math>. The canonical line bundle on <math id="S5.I2.i4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is the restriction of <math id="S5.I2.i4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}E^{\vee}}(1)\otimes\omega_{\mathbb{P}^{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}E^{\vee}}(1)\otimes\omega_{\mathbb{P}^{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which contracts the line <math id="S5.I2.i4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=Z=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=Z=0</annotation></semantics></math> in the map <math id="S5.I2.i4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}E^{\vee}\to\mathbb{P}^{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}E^{\vee}\to\mathbb{P}^{5}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, <math id="S5.I2.i4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math> is contained in each of the planes spanned by the image of a fiber of <math id="S5.I2.i4.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> under the canoncial. Hence, the <math id="S5.I2.i4.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{1}_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mn>4</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{1}_{4}</annotation></semantics></math> plus <math id="S5.I2.i4.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="S5.I2.i4.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{2}_{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{2}_{5}</annotation></semantics></math>. The locus of genus <math id="S5.I2.i4.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>6</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6</annotation></semantics></math> curves possessing a <math id="S5.I2.i4.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{2}_{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{2}_{5}</annotation></semantics></math> is codimension <math id="S5.I2.i4.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S5.I2.i4.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{6}</annotation></semantics></math>, but this stratum has codimension <math id="S5.I2.i4.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S5.I2.i4.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{4,6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{4,6}</annotation></semantics></math> because projection from any point on a plane quintic gives a <math id="S5.I2.i4.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{1}_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mn>4</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{1}_{4}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I2.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(5)</span> 
<div id="S5.I2.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I2.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I2.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{e}=(1,4,4),\vec{f}=(2,7)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{e}=(1,4,4),\vec{f}=(2,7)</annotation></semantics></math>, (codimension <math id="S5.I2.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>): Hyperelliptic curves</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S5.Thmthm7.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The open <math id="S5.Thmthm7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{4,6}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{4,6}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is the union of strata (1), (2), and (3), while <math id="S5.Thmthm7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{4,6}^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{4,6}^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math> contains only the generic stratum (1).
The image in <math id="S5.Thmthm7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{g}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S5.Thmthm7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{4,6}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{4,6}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> under the forgetful map is what Penev–Vakil <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>]</cite> call the “Mukai general locus” of genus <math id="S5.Thmthm7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>6</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6</annotation></semantics></math> curves.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p18.1" class="ltx_p">Using the numerical results of Lemma <a href="#S5.Thmthm6" title="Proposition 5.6. ‣ 5.2. Degree 
          
            4 ‣ 5. The good opens and codimension bounds ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.6</span></a>, we show that the codimension of <span id="S5.SS2.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">non-factoring</span> covers that fail our cohomological condition grows as a positive fraction of the genus.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmthm8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5.8</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmthm8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The locus of non-factoring degree <math id="S5.Thmthm8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> covers <math id="S5.Thmthm8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha:C\rightarrow\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha:C\rightarrow\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},F_{\alpha}^{\vee}\otimes\Sym^{2}E_{\alpha}\otimes\mathcal{O}(-2))&gt;0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi><mo>∨</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Sym</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},F_{\alpha}^{\vee}\otimes\Sym^{2}E_{\alpha}\otimes\mathcal{O}(-2))&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.Thmthm8.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm8.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">has codimension at least <math id="S5.Thmthm8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{g+3}{4}-4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{g+3}{4}-4</annotation></semantics></math>. That is, the codimension the complement of <math id="S5.Thmthm8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}^{\circ}_{4,g}\cap\mathcal{H}^{\mathrm{nf}}_{4,g}\subset\mathcal{H}^{\mathrm{nf}}_{4,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo>∩</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>nf</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>nf</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}^{\circ}_{4,g}\cap\mathcal{H}^{\mathrm{nf}}_{4,g}\subset\mathcal{H}^{\mathrm{nf}}_{4,g}</annotation></semantics></math> is at least <math id="S5.Thmthm8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{g+3}{4}-4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{g+3}{4}-4</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.6" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS2.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">By equation (<a href="#S5.E9" title="In 5.2. Degree 
          
            4 ‣ 5. The good opens and codimension bounds ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.9</span></a>), the codimension of the locus of covers <math id="S5.SS2.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S5.SS2.p19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\alpha}=\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\alpha}=\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p19.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\alpha}=\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\alpha}=\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})</annotation></semantics></math>
is</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle u(\vec{e},\vec{f})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle u(\vec{e},\vec{f})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{E}nd(\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})))+h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{E}nd(\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})))-h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})^{\vee}\otimes\Sym^{2}\mathcal{O}(\vec{e}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Sym</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{E}nd(\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})))+h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{E}nd(\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})))-h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})^{\vee}\otimes\Sym^{2}\mathcal{O}(\vec{e}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq 2e_{3}-2e_{1}+f_{2}-f_{1}-4-h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})^{\vee}\otimes\Sym^{2}\mathcal{O}(\vec{e}))." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Sym</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq 2e_{3}-2e_{1}+f_{2}-f_{1}-4-h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})^{\vee}\otimes\Sym^{2}\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p19.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p19.2.1" class="ltx_text">Assuming <math id="S5.SS2.p19.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> does not factor, Proposition <a href="#S5.Thmthm6" title="Proposition 5.6. ‣ 5.2. Degree 
          
            4 ‣ 5. The good opens and codimension bounds ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.6</span></a> (2) and (3) show that the only summands of <math id="S5.SS2.p19.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})^{\vee}\otimes\Sym^{2}\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Sym</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})^{\vee}\otimes\Sym^{2}\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})</annotation></semantics></math> that can contribute to <math id="S5.SS2.p19.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})^{\vee}\otimes\Sym^{2}\mathcal{O}(\vec{e}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Sym</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})^{\vee}\otimes\Sym^{2}\mathcal{O}(\vec{e}))</annotation></semantics></math> are <math id="S5.SS2.p19.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(2e_{1}-f_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(2e_{1}-f_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p19.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(e_{1}+e_{2}-f_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(e_{1}+e_{2}-f_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus, our task is to bound the function</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2e_{3}-2e_{1}+f_{2}-f_{1}-4-\max\{0,f_{2}-2e_{1}-1\}-\max\{0,f_{2}-e_{1}-e_{2}-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2e_{3}-2e_{1}+f_{2}-f_{1}-4-\max\{0,f_{2}-2e_{1}-1\}-\max\{0,f_{2}-e_{1}-e_{2}-1\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p19.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p19.3.1" class="ltx_text">from below on the region where the conditions of Proposition <a href="#S5.Thmthm6" title="Proposition 5.6. ‣ 5.2. Degree 
          
            4 ‣ 5. The good opens and codimension bounds ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.6</span></a> hold and <math id="S5.SS2.p19.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2e_{1}-f_{2}\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2e_{1}-f_{2}\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, which is equivalent to <math id="S5.SS2.p19.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})^{\vee}\otimes\Sym^{2}\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})\otimes\mathcal{O}(-2))&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Sym</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})^{\vee}\otimes\Sym^{2}\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})\otimes\mathcal{O}(-2))&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p20" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let us introduce a function of <math id="S5.SS2.p20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> real variables</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(x_{1},x_{2},x_{3},y_{1},y_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(x_{1},x_{2},x_{3},y_{1},y_{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=2x_{3}-2x_{1}+y_{2}-y_{1}-\max\{0,y_{2}-2x_{1}\}-\max\{0,y_{2}-x_{1}-x_{2}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=2x_{3}-2x_{1}+y_{2}-y_{1}-\max\{0,y_{2}-2x_{1}\}-\max\{0,y_{2}-x_{1}-x_{2}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p20.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p20.2.1" class="ltx_text">so that</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u(\vec{e},\vec{f})\geq(g+3)f\left(\frac{e_{1}}{g+3},\frac{e_{2}}{g+3},\frac{e_{3}}{g+3},\frac{f_{1}}{g+3},\frac{f_{2}}{g+3}\right)-4." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(\vec{e},\vec{f})\geq(g+3)f\left(\frac{e_{1}}{g+3},\frac{e_{2}}{g+3},\frac{e_{3}}{g+3},\frac{f_{1}}{g+3},\frac{f_{2}}{g+3}\right)-4.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p20.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p20.3.1" class="ltx_text">We wish to minimize <math id="S5.SS2.p20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> on the compact region defined by</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle x_{1}+x_{2}+x_{3}=1,\quad y_{1}+y_{2}=1,\quad 0\leq x_{1}\leq x_{2}\leq x_{3},\quad 0\leq y_{1}\leq 2x_{1}\leq y_{2}\leq 2x_{2},x_{1}+x_{3}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>3</mn></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{1}+x_{2}+x_{3}=1,\quad y_{1}+y_{2}=1,\quad 0\leq x_{1}\leq x_{2}\leq x_{3},\quad 0\leq y_{1}\leq 2x_{1}\leq y_{2}\leq 2x_{2},x_{1}+x_{3}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p20.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p20.4.1" class="ltx_text">These correspond to the conditions from Proposition <a href="#S5.Thmthm6" title="Proposition 5.6. ‣ 5.2. Degree 
          
            4 ‣ 5. The good opens and codimension bounds ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.6</span></a>, together with the condition that <math id="S5.SS2.p20.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2e_{1}\leq f_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2e_{1}\leq f_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, which must be satisfied if the cohomological condition is failed.
Since <math id="S5.SS2.p20.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is piecewise linear, its extreme values are attained where multiple boundary conditions (including those where the function changes) intersect at a point.
A program provied in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite> performs the linear algebra to locate such points and evaluates <math id="S5.SS2.p20.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> at them to determine its minimum. The minimum is <math id="S5.SS2.p20.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{4}</annotation></semantics></math>, attained at <math id="S5.SS2.p20.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{1},x_{2},x_{3},y_{1},y_{2})=(\frac{1}{4},\frac{3}{8},\frac{3}{8},\frac{1}{2},\frac{1}{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{1},x_{2},x_{3},y_{1},y_{2})=(\frac{1}{4},\frac{3}{8},\frac{3}{8},\frac{1}{2},\frac{1}{2})</annotation></semantics></math>. It follows that, if <math id="S5.SS2.p20.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})^{\vee}\otimes\Sym^{2}\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})\otimes\mathcal{O}(-2))&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Sym</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})^{\vee}\otimes\Sym^{2}\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})\otimes\mathcal{O}(-2))&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S5.SS2.p20.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u(\vec{e},\vec{f})\geq\frac{g+3}{4}-4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(\vec{e},\vec{f})\geq\frac{g+3}{4}-4</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmthm9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 5.9</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmthm9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Aaron Landesman points out that our above Lemma <a href="#S5.Thmthm8" title="Lemma 5.8. ‣ 5.2. Degree 
          
            4 ‣ 5. The good opens and codimension bounds ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.8</span></a> parallels <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>, Lemma 11]</cite> of Bhargava. Bhargava’s two cases <math id="S5.Thmthm9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{11}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{11}=0</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S5.Thmthm9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{11}=a_{12}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>12</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{11}=a_{12}=0</annotation></semantics></math> correspond to the fact that either <math id="S5.Thmthm9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(2e_{1}-f_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(2e_{1}-f_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S5.Thmthm9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(2e_{1}-f_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(2e_{1}-f_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.Thmthm9.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(e_{1}+e_{2}-f_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(e_{1}+e_{2}-f_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> are the only possible negative summands of <math id="S5.Thmthm9.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\alpha}^{\vee}\otimes\Sym^{2}E_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi><mo>∨</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Sym</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\alpha}^{\vee}\otimes\Sym^{2}E_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> for a non-factoring cover <math id="S5.Thmthm9.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p21" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p21.1" class="ltx_p">Lemmas <a href="#S5.Thmthm5" title="Lemma 5.5. ‣ 5.2. Degree 
          
            4 ‣ 5. The good opens and codimension bounds ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.5</span></a> and <a href="#S5.Thmthm8" title="Lemma 5.8. ‣ 5.2. Degree 
          
            4 ‣ 5. The good opens and codimension bounds ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.8</span></a> together should be thought of as saying that <math id="S5.SS2.p21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\mathrm{nf}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>nf</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\mathrm{nf}}</annotation></semantics></math> are “good approximations” of each other. We can now complete the proof of Theorem <a href="#S1.Thmthm2" title="Theorem 1.2. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.7" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#S1.Thmthm2" title="Theorem 1.2. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS2.p22" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p22.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p22.1.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose <math id="S5.SS2.p22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i&lt;\frac{g+3}{4}-4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i&lt;\frac{g+3}{4}-4</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider the restriction maps</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{i}(\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\mathrm{nf}})\xrightarrow{\sim}A^{i}(\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\mathrm{nf}}\cap\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\circ})\xleftarrow{\sim}A^{i}(\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\circ})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>nf</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo></mover><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>nf</mi></msubsup><mo>∩</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>←</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo></mover><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{i}(\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\mathrm{nf}})\xrightarrow{\sim}A^{i}(\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\mathrm{nf}}\cap\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\circ})\xleftarrow{\sim}A^{i}(\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\circ}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p22.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p22.2.1" class="ltx_text">Lemma <a href="#S5.Thmthm8" title="Lemma 5.8. ‣ 5.2. Degree 
          
            4 ‣ 5. The good opens and codimension bounds ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.8</span></a> says the arrow on the left is an isomorphism; Lemma <a href="#S5.Thmthm5" title="Lemma 5.5. ‣ 5.2. Degree 
          
            4 ‣ 5. The good opens and codimension bounds ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.5</span></a> says the arrow on the right is an isomorphism.
In turn then, we also have</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{i}(\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\mathrm{nf}})\xrightarrow{\sim}R^{i}(\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\mathrm{nf}}\cap\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\circ})\xleftarrow{\sim}R^{i}(\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\circ})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>nf</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo></mover><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>nf</mi></msubsup><mo>∩</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>←</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo></mover><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{i}(\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\mathrm{nf}})\xrightarrow{\sim}R^{i}(\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\mathrm{nf}}\cap\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\circ})\xleftarrow{\sim}R^{i}(\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\circ}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p22.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p22.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S5.SS2.p22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> of an open substack of <math id="S5.SS2.p22.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{4,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{4,g}</annotation></semantics></math> means the image of tautological classes under the restriction to that open.
Since <math id="S5.SS2.p22.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\circ}\subset\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo>⊂</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\circ}\subset\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, Lemma <a href="#S5.Thmthm3" title="Lemma 5.3. ‣ 5.2. Degree 
          
            4 ‣ 5. The good opens and codimension bounds ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a> implies <math id="S5.SS2.p22.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{i}(\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\circ})=R^{i}(\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\circ})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{i}(\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\circ})=R^{i}(\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\circ})</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, we conclude</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{i}(\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\mathrm{nf}})=A^{i}(\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\circ})=R^{i}(\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\circ})=R^{i}(\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\mathrm{nf}}).\qed" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>nf</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>nf</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" lspace="0.0835em" mathvariant="italic" separator="true">∎</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{i}(\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\mathrm{nf}})=A^{i}(\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\circ})=R^{i}(\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\circ})=R^{i}(\mathcal{H}_{4,g}^{\mathrm{nf}}).\qed</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.3. </span>Degree <math id="S5.SS3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="S5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Using Casnati’s characterization of regular degree <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> covers (Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmthm8" title="Theorem 3.8 (Casnati). ‣ 3.3. The category of regular pentagonal covers ‣ 3. The Casnati–Ekedahl structure theorem ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.8</span></a>), a regular degree <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> cover of is equivalent to the data of a rank <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> vector bundle <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>; a rank <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> vector bundle <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>; an isomorphism <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\det E)^{\otimes 2}\cong\det F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.1389em">≅</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\det E)^{\otimes 2}\cong\det F</annotation></semantics></math>; and a global section of <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{H}om(E^{\vee}\otimes\det E,\wedge^{2}F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>E</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em">∧</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}om(E^{\vee}\otimes\det E,\wedge^{2}F)</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying certain conditions.
By Example <a href="#S3.Thmthm1" title="Example 3.1 (Covers of 
          
            
              
              P
              1
            
          
        ). ‣ 3. The Casnati–Ekedahl structure theorem ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, if a cover <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha:C\to\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha:C\to\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> has genus <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg(E_{\alpha})=g+4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg(E_{\alpha})=g+4</annotation></semantics></math>. In turn, <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg(F_{\alpha})=2\deg(E_{\alpha})=2g+8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg(F_{\alpha})=2\deg(E_{\alpha})=2g+8</annotation></semantics></math>.
To build the appropriate base stack, we start with <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{4,g+4}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{5,2g+8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>BSL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{4,g+4}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{5,2g+8}</annotation></semantics></math> which parametrizes tuples <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(S,V,E,F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S,V,E,F)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> is a rank <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> vector bundle on <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> with trivial determinant, and <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> are vector bundles of the appropriate ranks and degrees on <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}V</annotation></semantics></math>. We let <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the universal rank <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> vector bundle and <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> the universal rank <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> bundle on the universal <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-bundle <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi:\mathcal{P}\to\mathcal{V}_{4,g+4}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{5,2g+8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>BSL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi:\mathcal{P}\to\mathcal{V}_{4,g+4}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{5,2g+8}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\det\mathcal{E}^{\otimes 2}\otimes\det\mathcal{F}^{\vee}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\det\mathcal{E}^{\otimes 2}\otimes\det\mathcal{F}^{\vee}</annotation></semantics></math> is a line bundle of degree <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> on each fiber of <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\det\mathcal{E}^{\otimes 2}\otimes\det\mathcal{F}^{\vee}\cong\pi^{*}\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\det\mathcal{E}^{\otimes 2}\otimes\det\mathcal{F}^{\vee}\cong\pi^{*}\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> where
<math id="S5.SS3.p1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}:=\pi_{*}(\det\mathcal{E}^{\otimes 2}\otimes\det\mathcal{F}^{\vee})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}:=\pi_{*}(\det\mathcal{E}^{\otimes 2}\otimes\det\mathcal{F}^{\vee}),</annotation></semantics></math>
which is a line bundle by cohomology and base change.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmthm10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 5.10</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmthm10.p1.1" class="ltx_p">With notation as above, we define the stack <math id="S5.Thmthm10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{5,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{5,g}</annotation></semantics></math> as the <math id="S5.Thmthm10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{G}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔾</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{G}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>-torsor over <math id="S5.Thmthm10.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{5,g+4}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{5,2g+8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>BSL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{5,g+4}\times_{\BSL_{2}}\mathcal{V}_{5,2g+8}</annotation></semantics></math> given by the complement of the zero section of the line bundle <math id="S5.Thmthm10.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">By slight abuse of notation, we continue to denote the universal <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi:\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi:\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-bundle by <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}\to\mathcal{B}_{5,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}\to\mathcal{B}_{5,g}</annotation></semantics></math> and the universal rank <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> vector bundles on it by <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=\mathcal{O}_{\mathcal{P}}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=\mathcal{O}_{\mathcal{P}}(1)</annotation></semantics></math> and write</p>
<table id="S5.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}(\mathcal{E})=\pi^{*}a_{i}+(\pi^{*}a_{i}^{\prime})z\qquad\text{and}\qquad c_{i}(\mathcal{F})=\pi^{*}b_{i}+(\pi^{*}b_{i}^{\prime})z." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}(\mathcal{E})=\pi^{*}a_{i}+(\pi^{*}a_{i}^{\prime})z\qquad\text{and}\qquad c_{i}(\mathcal{F})=\pi^{*}b_{i}+(\pi^{*}b_{i}^{\prime})z.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">for <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i},b_{i}\in A^{i}(\mathcal{B}_{5,g})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i},b_{i}\in A^{i}(\mathcal{B}_{5,g})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}^{\prime},b_{i}^{\prime}\in A^{i-1}(\mathcal{B}_{5,g})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}^{\prime},b_{i}^{\prime}\in A^{i-1}(\mathcal{B}_{5,g})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Note that <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2a_{1}^{\prime}=b_{1}^{\prime}=2(g+4)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2a_{1}^{\prime}=b_{1}^{\prime}=2(g+4)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Moreover, by definition of <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{5,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{5,g}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}(\det\mathcal{E}^{\otimes 2}\otimes\det\mathcal{F}^{\vee})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}(\det\mathcal{E}^{\otimes 2}\otimes\det\mathcal{F}^{\vee})=0</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{1}=2a_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{1}=2a_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Using Lemma <a href="#S2.Thmthm1" title="Lemma 2.1. ‣ 2.2. (Equivariant) Intersection Theory ‣ 2. Notation and conventions ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a> and Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmthm4" title="Theorem 4.4. ‣ 4.1. The rational Chow ring ‣ 4. Pairs of vector bundles on 
        
          
            
            P
            1
          
        
      -bundles ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a> as in the previous subsection, we have</p>
<table id="S5.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(5.10)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\trun^{g+5}A^{*}(\mathcal{B}_{5,g})=\trun^{g+5}\mathbb{Q}[c_{2},a_{1},\ldots,a_{4},a_{2}^{\prime},\ldots,a_{4}^{\prime},b_{2},\ldots,b_{5},b_{2}^{\prime},\ldots,b_{5}^{\prime}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Trun</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Trun</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>5</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\trun^{g+5}A^{*}(\mathcal{B}_{5,g})=\trun^{g+5}\mathbb{Q}[c_{2},a_{1},\ldots,a_{4},a_{2}^{\prime},\ldots,a_{4}^{\prime},b_{2},\ldots,b_{5},b_{2}^{\prime},\ldots,b_{5}^{\prime}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We define <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{5,g}:=\mathcal{H}om(\mathcal{E}^{\vee}\otimes\det\mathcal{E},\wedge^{2}\mathcal{F})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em">∧</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{5,g}:=\mathcal{H}om(\mathcal{E}^{\vee}\otimes\det\mathcal{E},\wedge^{2}\mathcal{F})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{5,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{5,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{5,g}^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{5,g}^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math> as in (<a href="#S5.E1" title="In 5. The good opens and codimension bounds ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>) and (<a href="#S5.E2" title="In 5. The good opens and codimension bounds ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>), respectively.
Given a map <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\rightarrow\mathcal{H}_{5,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\rightarrow\mathcal{H}_{5,g}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{S}:\mathcal{P}_{S}\rightarrow S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{S}:\mathcal{P}_{S}\rightarrow S</annotation></semantics></math> denote the <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-bundle and let <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{S}</annotation></semantics></math> (resp. <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{S})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{S})</annotation></semantics></math> be the rank <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> (resp. rank <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math>) vector bundle on <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{S}</annotation></semantics></math> associated to the family in the sense of Casnati–Ekedahl.
The open substacks <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}^{\circ}_{5,g}\subseteq\mathcal{H}^{\prime}_{5,g}\subseteq\mathcal{H}_{5,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo>⊆</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}^{\circ}_{5,g}\subseteq\mathcal{H}^{\prime}_{5,g}\subseteq\mathcal{H}_{5,g}</annotation></semantics></math> are defined by</p>
<table id="S5.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\{S\rightarrow\mathcal{H}^{\circ}_{5,g}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\{S\rightarrow\mathcal{H}^{\circ}_{5,g}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex27.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\{S\rightarrow\mathcal{H}_{5,g}:R^{1}(\pi_{S})_{*}(\mathcal{H}om(\mathcal{E}^{\vee}_{S}\otimes\det\mathcal{E}_{S},\wedge^{2}\mathcal{F}_{S})\otimes\mathcal{O}_{\mathcal{P}_{S}}(-2))=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>∨</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em">∧</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\{S\rightarrow\mathcal{H}_{5,g}:R^{1}(\pi_{S})_{*}(\mathcal{H}om(\mathcal{E}^{\vee}_{S}\otimes\det\mathcal{E}_{S},\wedge^{2}\mathcal{F}_{S})\otimes\mathcal{O}_{\mathcal{P}_{S}}(-2))=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\text{and $\mathcal{F}_{S}$ globally generated on fibers of $\pi_{S}$}\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>and </mtext><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mtext> globally generated on fibers of </mtext><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\text{and $\mathcal{F}_{S}$ globally generated on fibers of $\pi_{S}$}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\{S\rightarrow\mathcal{H}^{\prime}_{5,g}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\{S\rightarrow\mathcal{H}^{\prime}_{5,g}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex29.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\{S\rightarrow\mathcal{H}_{5,g}:R^{1}(\pi_{S})_{*}(\mathcal{H}om(\mathcal{E}^{\vee}_{S}\otimes\det\mathcal{E}_{S},\wedge^{2}\mathcal{F}_{S}))=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>∨</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em">∧</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\{S\rightarrow\mathcal{H}_{5,g}:R^{1}(\pi_{S})_{*}(\mathcal{H}om(\mathcal{E}^{\vee}_{S}\otimes\det\mathcal{E}_{S},\wedge^{2}\mathcal{F}_{S}))=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\text{and $\mathcal{F}_{S}$ globally generated on fibers of $\pi_{S}$}\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>and </mtext><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mtext> globally generated on fibers of </mtext><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\text{and $\mathcal{F}_{S}$ globally generated on fibers of $\pi_{S}$}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The important feature of the open <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{5,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{5,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is that it can be realized as an open inside the vector bundle <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{5,g}^{\prime}:=\pi_{*}\mathcal{U}_{5,g}|_{\mathcal{B}_{5,g}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{5,g}^{\prime}:=\pi_{*}\mathcal{U}_{5,g}|_{\mathcal{B}_{5,g}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{5,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{5,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmthm11" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5.11</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmthm11.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There is an open inclusion <math id="S5.Thmthm11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{5,g}^{\prime}\to\mathcal{X}_{5,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{5,g}^{\prime}\to\mathcal{X}_{5,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, <math id="S5.Thmthm11.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\mathcal{H}_{5,g}^{\prime})=R^{*}(\mathcal{H}_{5,g}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\mathcal{H}_{5,g}^{\prime})=R^{*}(\mathcal{H}_{5,g}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> is generated by the CE classes <math id="S5.Thmthm11.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2},a_{1},\ldots,a_{4},a_{2}^{\prime},\ldots,a_{4}^{\prime},b_{2},\ldots,b_{5},b_{2}^{\prime},\ldots,b_{5}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>5</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2},a_{1},\ldots,a_{4},a_{2}^{\prime},\ldots,a_{4}^{\prime},b_{2},\ldots,b_{5},b_{2}^{\prime},\ldots,b_{5}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">The objects of <math id="S5.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{5,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{5,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> are tuples <math id="S5.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(S,V,E,F,\phi,\eta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S,V,E,F,\phi,\eta)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S5.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(S,V,E,F,\phi)\in\mathcal{B}_{5,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S,V,E,F,\phi)\in\mathcal{B}_{5,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\eta\in H^{0}(\mathbb{P}V,\mathcal{H}om(E^{\vee}\otimes\det E,\wedge^{2}F))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>E</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em">∧</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\in H^{0}(\mathbb{P}V,\mathcal{H}om(E^{\vee}\otimes\det E,\wedge^{2}F))</annotation></semantics></math>. Using the notation of Section <a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3. The category of regular pentagonal covers ‣ 3. The Casnati–Ekedahl structure theorem ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>, we define <math id="S5.SS3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}_{5,g}^{\prime}\subset\mathcal{X}_{5,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>⊂</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}_{5,g}^{\prime}\subset\mathcal{X}_{5,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> to be the open substack defined by the condition that <math id="S5.SS3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(\Phi(\eta))\subset\mathbb{P}E^{\vee}\to S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(\Phi(\eta))\subset\mathbb{P}E^{\vee}\to S</annotation></semantics></math> is a family of smooth curves. Considering their Hilbert polynomials as determined by the resolution (<a href="#S3.E14" title="In 3.3. The category of regular pentagonal covers ‣ 3. The Casnati–Ekedahl structure theorem ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.14</span></a>), we see that the fibers of <math id="S5.SS3.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(\Phi(\eta))\to S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(\Phi(\eta))\to S</annotation></semantics></math> have arithmetic genus <math id="S5.SS3.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>.
Applying Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmthm8" title="Theorem 3.8 (Casnati). ‣ 3.3. The category of regular pentagonal covers ‣ 3. The Casnati–Ekedahl structure theorem ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.8</span></a>, we see that <math id="S5.SS3.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{5,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{5,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is equivalent to <math id="S5.SS3.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}_{5,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}_{5,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">By excision, the Chow ring of <math id="S5.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{5,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{5,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is generated by restriction of classes from <math id="S5.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{5,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{5,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S5.SS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{5,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{5,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is a vector bundle over <math id="S5.SS3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{5,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{5,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, their Chow rings are isomorphic, so the statement about generators follows from Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmthm4" title="Theorem 4.4. ‣ 4.1. The rational Chow ring ‣ 4. Pairs of vector bundles on 
        
          
            
            P
            1
          
        
      -bundles ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Now we show that the complements of the opens we have defined have high codimension.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmthm12" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5.12</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmthm12.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm12.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The support of <math id="S5.Thmthm12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{1}\pi_{*}(\mathcal{U}_{5,g}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{\mathcal{P}}(-2))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{1}\pi_{*}(\mathcal{U}_{5,g}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{\mathcal{P}}(-2))</annotation></semantics></math> has codimension at least <math id="S5.Thmthm12.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{g+4}{5}-16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{g+4}{5}-16</annotation></semantics></math>. That is, the codimension of the complement of <math id="S5.Thmthm12.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{5,g}^{\circ}\subset\mathcal{B}_{5,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{5,g}^{\circ}\subset\mathcal{B}_{5,g}</annotation></semantics></math> is at least <math id="S5.Thmthm12.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{g+4}{5}-16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{g+4}{5}-16</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">By (<a href="#S4.E7" title="In 4.2. Splitting loci ‣ 4. Pairs of vector bundles on 
        
          
            
            P
            1
          
        
      -bundles ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.7</span></a>), the codimension of the support of <math id="S5.SS3.p8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R^{1}\pi_{*}(\mathcal{H}om(\mathcal{E}^{\vee}\otimes\det\mathcal{E},\wedge^{2}\mathcal{F})\otimes\mathcal{O}_{\mathcal{P}}(-2))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><msub><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em">∧</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{1}\pi_{*}(\mathcal{H}om(\mathcal{E}^{\vee}\otimes\det\mathcal{E},\wedge^{2}\mathcal{F})\otimes\mathcal{O}_{\mathcal{P}}(-2))</annotation></semantics></math> is the minimum value of</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{E}nd(\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})))+h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{E}nd(\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{E}nd(\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})))+h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{E}nd(\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">as we range over splitting types <math id="S5.SS3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{e}</annotation></semantics></math> of degree <math id="S5.SS3.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g+4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g+4</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS3.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{f}</annotation></semantics></math> of degree <math id="S5.SS3.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2g+8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2g+8</annotation></semantics></math> so that</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{H}om(\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})^{\vee}\otimes\det\mathcal{O}(\vec{e}),\wedge^{2}\mathcal{O}(\vec{f}))\otimes\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{1}}(-2))&gt;0\quad\Leftrightarrow\quad e_{1}+f_{1}+f_{2}-(g+4)\leq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∨</mo></msup><mo>⊗</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em">∧</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{H}om(\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})^{\vee}\otimes\det\mathcal{O}(\vec{e}),\wedge^{2}\mathcal{O}(\vec{f}))\otimes\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{1}}(-2))&gt;0\quad\Leftrightarrow\quad e_{1}+f_{1}+f_{2}-(g+4)\leq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Similar to the proof of Lemma <a href="#S5.Thmthm4" title="Lemma 5.4. ‣ 5.2. Degree 
          
            4 ‣ 5. The good opens and codimension bounds ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.4</span></a>, we may find this minimum by finding the minimum of the function</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x_{1},\ldots,x_{4},y_{1},\ldots,y_{5})=3x_{4}+x_{3}-x_{2}-3x_{1}+4y_{5}+2y_{4}-2y_{2}-4y_{1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x_{1},\ldots,x_{4},y_{1},\ldots,y_{5})=3x_{4}+x_{3}-x_{2}-3x_{1}+4y_{5}+2y_{4}-2y_{2}-4y_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">on the compact region <math id="S5.SS3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> defined by</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 0\leq x_{1}\leq\cdots\leq x_{4},\quad x_{1}+\ldots+x_{4}=1,\quad 0\leq y_{1}\leq\cdots\leq y_{5},\quad y_{1}+\ldots+y_{5}=2" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 0\leq x_{1}\leq\cdots\leq x_{4},\quad x_{1}+\ldots+x_{4}=1,\quad 0\leq y_{1}\leq\cdots\leq y_{5},\quad y_{1}+\ldots+y_{5}=2</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{1}+y_{1}+y_{2}-1\leq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{1}+y_{1}+y_{2}-1\leq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">Using our code <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite>,
we find that the minimum of the linear function <math id="S5.SS3.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S5.SS3.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S5.SS3.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{5}</annotation></semantics></math> attained at
<math id="S5.SS3.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\frac{1}{5},\frac{4}{15},\frac{4}{15},\frac{4}{15},\frac{2}{5},\frac{2}{5},\frac{2}{5},\frac{2}{5},\frac{2}{5})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>15</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>15</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>15</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\frac{1}{5},\frac{4}{15},\frac{4}{15},\frac{4}{15},\frac{2}{5},\frac{2}{5},\frac{2}{5},\frac{2}{5},\frac{2}{5})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus,</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dim\Supp R^{1}\pi_{*}(\mathcal{U}_{5,g}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{\mathcal{P}}(-2))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">dim</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Supp</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dim\Supp R^{1}\pi_{*}(\mathcal{U}_{5,g}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{\mathcal{P}}(-2))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex36.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq(g+4)\cdot\min_{D}(f)-16=\frac{g+4}{5}-16.\qed" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>D</mi></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" lspace="0.0835em" mathvariant="italic" separator="true">∎</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq(g+4)\cdot\min_{D}(f)-16=\frac{g+4}{5}-16.\qed</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p10.1" class="ltx_p">For later use, let us note an immediate consequence of the previous lemma: Using excision and (<a href="#S5.E10" title="In 5.3. Degree 
          
            5 ‣ 5. The good opens and codimension bounds ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.10</span></a>), we see</p>
<table id="S5.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(5.11)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\trun^{(g+4)/5-16}A^{*}(\mathcal{B}_{5,g}^{\circ})=\trun^{(g+4)/5-16}\mathbb{Q}[c_{2},a_{1},\ldots,a_{4},a_{2}^{\prime},\ldots,a_{4}^{\prime},b_{2},\ldots,b_{5},b_{2}^{\prime},\ldots,b_{5}^{\prime}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Trun</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Trun</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>5</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\trun^{(g+4)/5-16}A^{*}(\mathcal{B}_{5,g}^{\circ})=\trun^{(g+4)/5-16}\mathbb{Q}[c_{2},a_{1},\ldots,a_{4},a_{2}^{\prime},\ldots,a_{4}^{\prime},b_{2},\ldots,b_{5},b_{2}^{\prime},\ldots,b_{5}^{\prime}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmthm13" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5.13</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm13.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmthm13.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm13.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The codimension of the locus of smooth degree <math id="S5.Thmthm13.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> covers <math id="S5.Thmthm13.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="h^{1}(\mathcal{H}om(E_{\alpha}^{\vee}\otimes\det E_{\alpha},\wedge^{2}F_{\alpha})\otimes\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{1}}(-2))&gt;0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi><mo>∨</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em">∧</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{1}(\mathcal{H}om(E_{\alpha}^{\vee}\otimes\det E_{\alpha},\wedge^{2}F_{\alpha})\otimes\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{1}}(-2))&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.Thmthm13.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm13.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">has codimension at least <math id="S5.Thmthm13.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{g+4}{5}-16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{g+4}{5}-16</annotation></semantics></math>. That is, the codimension of the complement of <math id="S5.Thmthm13.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}^{\circ}_{5,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}^{\circ}_{5,g}</annotation></semantics></math> inside <math id="S5.Thmthm13.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{5,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{5,g}</annotation></semantics></math> is at least <math id="S5.Thmthm13.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{g+4}{5}-16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{g+4}{5}-16</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS3.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">The cohomological statement depends only on the splitting type of <math id="S5.SS3.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS3.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>.
In the proof of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>, Proposition 5.2]</cite>, Deopurkar–Patel show that
the codimension of the locus of covers such that <math id="S5.SS3.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\alpha}\cong\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\alpha}\cong\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS3.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\alpha}\cong\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\alpha}\cong\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})</annotation></semantics></math> has codimension</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(5.12)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle u(\vec{e},\vec{f})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle u(\vec{e},\vec{f})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{E}nd(\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})))+h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{E}nd(\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{E}nd(\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})))+h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{E}nd(\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad-h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})\otimes\wedge^{2}\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})\otimes\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{1}}(-g-4))." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">⊗</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em">∧</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad-h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})\otimes\wedge^{2}\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})\otimes\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{1}}(-g-4)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">A cover with these discrete invariants corresponds to a global section <math id="S5.SS3.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> of</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{H}om(\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})^{\vee}\otimes\det\mathcal{O}(\vec{e}),\wedge^{2}\mathcal{O}(\vec{f}))=\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})\otimes\wedge^{2}\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})\otimes\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{1}}(-g-4)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∨</mo></msup><mo>⊗</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em">∧</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">⊗</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em">∧</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}om(\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})^{\vee}\otimes\det\mathcal{O}(\vec{e}),\wedge^{2}\mathcal{O}(\vec{f}))=\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})\otimes\wedge^{2}\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})\otimes\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{1}}(-g-4).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p12.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p12.2.1" class="ltx_text">Such a global section can be represented by a skew-symmetric matrix</span></p>
<table id="S5.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(5.13)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\eta}=\left(\begin{matrix}0&amp;L_{1,2}&amp;L_{1,3}&amp;L_{1,4}&amp;L_{1,5}\\
-L_{1,2}&amp;0&amp;L_{2,3}&amp;L_{2,4}&amp;L_{2,5}\\
-L_{1,3}&amp;-L_{2,3}&amp;0&amp;L_{3,4}&amp;L_{3,5}\\
-L_{1,4}&amp;-L_{2,4}&amp;-L_{3,4}&amp;0&amp;L_{4,5}\\
-L_{1,5}&amp;-L_{2,5}&amp;-L_{3,5}&amp;-L_{4,5}&amp;0\end{matrix}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\eta}=\left(\begin{matrix}0&amp;L_{1,2}&amp;L_{1,3}&amp;L_{1,4}&amp;L_{1,5}\\
-L_{1,2}&amp;0&amp;L_{2,3}&amp;L_{2,4}&amp;L_{2,5}\\
-L_{1,3}&amp;-L_{2,3}&amp;0&amp;L_{3,4}&amp;L_{3,5}\\
-L_{1,4}&amp;-L_{2,4}&amp;-L_{3,4}&amp;0&amp;L_{4,5}\\
-L_{1,5}&amp;-L_{2,5}&amp;-L_{3,5}&amp;-L_{4,5}&amp;0\end{matrix}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p12.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p12.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S5.SS3.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{i,j}\in H^{0}(\mathcal{O}(f_{i}+f_{j})\otimes\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})\otimes\mathcal{O}(-g-4))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{i,j}\in H^{0}(\mathcal{O}(f_{i}+f_{j})\otimes\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})\otimes\mathcal{O}(-g-4))</annotation></semantics></math>.
The corresponding curve <math id="S5.SS3.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subset\mathbb{P}E^{\vee}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subset\mathbb{P}E^{\vee}</annotation></semantics></math> is cut out by the <math id="S5.SS3.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\times 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\times 4</annotation></semantics></math> Pfaffians of the main minors of <math id="S5.SS3.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>. The Pfaffian of the submatrix obtained by deleting the last row and column is</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{5}=L_{1,2}L_{3,4}-L_{1,3}L_{2,4}+L_{2,3}L_{1,4}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{5}=L_{1,2}L_{3,4}-L_{1,3}L_{2,4}+L_{2,3}L_{1,4}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p12.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p12.4.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="S5.SS3.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{5}</annotation></semantics></math> is reducible, then <math id="S5.SS3.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is reducible. Indeed, if <math id="S5.SS3.p12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> were irreducible, it would be contained in one component of <math id="S5.SS3.p12.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{5}</annotation></semantics></math>, forcing every fiber to be contained in a hyperplane, violating the Geometric-Riemann-Roch theorem.
Therefore, as observed in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>, p. 21]</cite>, <math id="S5.SS3.p12.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{1,2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{1,2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS3.p12.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{1,3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{1,3}</annotation></semantics></math> cannot both be identically zero, and so</span></p>
<table id="S5.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(5.14)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{1}+f_{3}+e_{4}-(g+4)\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{1}+f_{3}+e_{4}-(g+4)\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p12.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p12.5.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S5.SS3.p12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1},\ldots,X_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1},\ldots,X_{4}</annotation></semantics></math> be coordinates on <math id="S5.SS3.p12.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}E^{\vee}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}E^{\vee}</annotation></semantics></math> corresponding to a choice of splitting <math id="S5.SS3.p12.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E\cong\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E\cong\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})</annotation></semantics></math>, so we think of <math id="S5.SS3.p12.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> as a linear form in <math id="S5.SS3.p12.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1},\ldots,X_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1},\ldots,X_{4}</annotation></semantics></math> where the coefficient of <math id="S5.SS3.p12.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is a section of <math id="S5.SS3.p12.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(f_{i}+f_{j})\otimes\mathcal{O}(e_{k})\otimes\mathcal{O}(-g-4)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(f_{i}+f_{j})\otimes\mathcal{O}(e_{k})\otimes\mathcal{O}(-g-4)</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. a homogeneous polynomial of degree <math id="S5.SS3.p12.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}+f_{j}+e_{k}-(g+4)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}+f_{j}+e_{k}-(g+4)</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S5.SS3.p12.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
If <math id="S5.SS3.p12.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{5}</annotation></semantics></math> is irreducible, it cannot be divisible by <math id="S5.SS3.p12.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{4}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Observe that if <math id="S5.SS3.p12.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}+f_{j}+e_{3}-(g+4)&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}+f_{j}+e_{3}-(g+4)&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, then the coefficients of <math id="S5.SS3.p12.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S5.SS3.p12.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\leq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\leq 3</annotation></semantics></math> vanish, so <math id="S5.SS3.p12.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{4}</annotation></semantics></math> divides <math id="S5.SS3.p12.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S5.SS3.p12.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{4}</annotation></semantics></math> divides <math id="S5.SS3.p12.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{1,2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{1,2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS3.p12.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{1,3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{1,3}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS3.p12.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{1,4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{1,4}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S5.SS3.p12.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{4}</annotation></semantics></math> divides <math id="S5.SS3.p12.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{5}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS3.p12.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{5}</annotation></semantics></math> is reducible. To prevent this, we must have</span></p>
<table id="S5.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(5.15)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{1}+f_{4}+e_{3}-(g+4)\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{1}+f_{4}+e_{3}-(g+4)\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p12.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p12.6.1" class="ltx_text">Similarly, if <math id="S5.SS3.p12.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{4}</annotation></semantics></math> divides <math id="S5.SS3.p12.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{1,2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{1,2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS3.p12.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{1,3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{1,3}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS3.p12.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{2,3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{2,3}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S5.SS3.p12.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{4}</annotation></semantics></math> divides <math id="S5.SS3.p12.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{5}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS3.p12.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{5}</annotation></semantics></math> is reducible. To prevent this, we must have</span></p>
<table id="S5.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(5.16)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{2}+f_{3}+e_{3}-(g+4)\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{2}+f_{3}+e_{3}-(g+4)\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">For splitting types satisfying (<a href="#S5.E14" title="In Proof. ‣ 5.3. Degree 
          
            5 ‣ 5. The good opens and codimension bounds ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.14</span></a>), (<a href="#S5.E15" title="In Proof. ‣ 5.3. Degree 
          
            5 ‣ 5. The good opens and codimension bounds ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.15</span></a>), and (<a href="#S5.E16" title="In Proof. ‣ 5.3. Degree 
          
            5 ‣ 5. The good opens and codimension bounds ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.16</span></a>), at most <math id="S5.SS3.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="11" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>11</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">11</annotation></semantics></math> of the <math id="S5.SS3.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="40" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>40</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">40</annotation></semantics></math> summands of the form <math id="S5.SS3.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(e_{i}+f_{j}+f_{k}-(g+4))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(e_{i}+f_{j}+f_{k}-(g+4))</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S5.SS3.p13.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})\otimes\wedge^{2}\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})\otimes\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{1}}(-g-4)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">⊗</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em">∧</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})\otimes\wedge^{2}\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})\otimes\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^{1}}(-g-4)</annotation></semantics></math> can be negative. For these allowed splitting types, we have</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle u(\vec{e},\vec{f})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle u(\vec{e},\vec{f})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex41.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{E}nd(\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})))+h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{E}nd(\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{E}nd(\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})))+h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{E}nd(\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad-\sum_{i=1}^{4}\max\{0,g+3-f_{1}-f_{2}-e_{i}\}-\sum_{i=1}^{3}\max\{0,g+3-f_{1}-f_{3}-e_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></munderover></mstyle><mi>max</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></munderover></mstyle><mi>max</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad-\sum_{i=1}^{4}\max\{0,g+3-f_{1}-f_{2}-e_{i}\}-\sum_{i=1}^{3}\max\{0,g+3-f_{1}-f_{3}-e_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad-\sum_{i=1}^{2}\max\{0,g+3-f_{1}-f_{4}-e_{i}\}-\sum_{i=1}^{2}\max\{0,g+3-f_{2}-f_{3}-e_{i}\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></munderover></mstyle><mi>max</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></munderover></mstyle><mi>max</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad-\sum_{i=1}^{2}\max\{0,g+3-f_{1}-f_{4}-e_{i}\}-\sum_{i=1}^{2}\max\{0,g+3-f_{2}-f_{3}-e_{i}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p13.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p13.2.1" class="ltx_text">We seek a lower bound on <math id="S5.SS3.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u(\vec{e},\vec{f})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(\vec{e},\vec{f})</annotation></semantics></math> given that <math id="S5.SS3.p13.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})\otimes\wedge^{2}\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})\otimes\mathcal{O}(-g-4)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">⊗</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em">∧</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})\otimes\wedge^{2}\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})\otimes\mathcal{O}(-g-4)</annotation></semantics></math> has a non-positive summand, i.e. in the region where <math id="S5.SS3.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{1}+f_{1}+f_{2}-(g+4)\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{1}+f_{1}+f_{2}-(g+4)\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Note that</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{E}nd(\mathcal{O}(\vec{e}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{E}nd(\mathcal{O}(\vec{e}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex44.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq 3e_{4}+e_{3}-e_{2}-3e_{1}-6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq 3e_{4}+e_{3}-e_{2}-3e_{1}-6</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{E}nd(\mathcal{O}(\vec{f}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{E}nd(\mathcal{O}(\vec{f}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex45.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq 4f_{5}+2f_{4}-2f_{2}-4f_{1}-10." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq 4f_{5}+2f_{4}-2f_{2}-4f_{1}-10.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let us define a function of <math id="S5.SS3.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>9</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9</annotation></semantics></math> real variables</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(x_{1},\ldots,x_{4},y_{1},\ldots,y_{5})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(x_{1},\ldots,x_{4},y_{1},\ldots,y_{5})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex46.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=3x_{4}+x_{3}-x_{2}-3x_{1}+4y_{5}+2y_{4}-2y_{2}-4y_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=3x_{4}+x_{3}-x_{2}-3x_{1}+4y_{5}+2y_{4}-2y_{2}-4y_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad-\sum_{i=1}^{4}\max\{0,1-y_{1}-y_{2}-x_{i}\}-\sum_{i=1}^{3}\max\{0,1-y_{1}-y_{3}-x_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></munderover></mstyle><mi>max</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></munderover></mstyle><mi>max</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad-\sum_{i=1}^{4}\max\{0,1-y_{1}-y_{2}-x_{i}\}-\sum_{i=1}^{3}\max\{0,1-y_{1}-y_{3}-x_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad-\sum_{i=1}^{2}\max\{0,1-y_{1}-y_{4}-x_{i}\}-\sum_{i=1}^{2}\max\{0,1-y_{2}-y_{3}-x_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></munderover></mstyle><mi>max</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></munderover></mstyle><mi>max</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad-\sum_{i=1}^{2}\max\{0,1-y_{1}-y_{4}-x_{i}\}-\sum_{i=1}^{2}\max\{0,1-y_{2}-y_{3}-x_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p14.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p14.2.1" class="ltx_text">so that</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u(\vec{e},\vec{f})\geq(g+4)f\left(\frac{e_{1}}{g+4},\ldots,\frac{e_{4}}{g+4},\frac{f_{1}}{g+4},\ldots,\frac{f_{5}}{g+4}\right)-16." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(\vec{e},\vec{f})\geq(g+4)f\left(\frac{e_{1}}{g+4},\ldots,\frac{e_{4}}{g+4},\frac{f_{1}}{g+4},\ldots,\frac{f_{5}}{g+4}\right)-16.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p14.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p14.3.1" class="ltx_text">Now we wish to find the minimum of <math id="S5.SS3.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> on the compact region defined by</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 0\leq x_{1}\leq\cdots\leq x_{4},\quad x_{1}+\ldots+x_{4}=1,\quad 0\leq y_{1}\leq\cdots\leq y_{5},\quad y_{1}+\ldots+y_{5}=2" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 0\leq x_{1}\leq\cdots\leq x_{4},\quad x_{1}+\ldots+x_{4}=1,\quad 0\leq y_{1}\leq\cdots\leq y_{5},\quad y_{1}+\ldots+y_{5}=2</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle y_{1}+y_{3}+x_{4}-1\geq 0,\quad y_{1}+y_{4}+x_{3}-1\geq 0,\qquad y_{2}+y_{3}+x_{3}-1\geq 0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle y_{1}+y_{3}+x_{4}-1\geq 0,\quad y_{1}+y_{4}+x_{3}-1\geq 0,\qquad y_{2}+y_{3}+x_{3}-1\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{1}+y_{1}+y_{2}-1\leq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{1}+y_{1}+y_{2}-1\leq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p14.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p14.4.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S5.SS3.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is piecewise linear, its extreme values are attained at points where multiple boundary conditions (including those where the linear function changes) intersect to give a single point. Our code <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite> performs the linear algebra to locate such points and determines that the minimum is <math id="S5.SS3.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{5}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is attained at <math id="S5.SS3.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\frac{1}{5},\frac{4}{15},\frac{4}{15},\frac{4}{15},\frac{2}{5},\frac{2}{5},\frac{2}{5},\frac{2}{5},\frac{2}{5})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>15</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>15</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>15</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\frac{1}{5},\frac{4}{15},\frac{4}{15},\frac{4}{15},\frac{2}{5},\frac{2}{5},\frac{2}{5},\frac{2}{5},\frac{2}{5})</annotation></semantics></math>.
It follows that if <math id="S5.SS3.p14.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{e}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS3.p14.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{f}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy <math id="S5.SS3.p14.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})\otimes\wedge^{2}\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})\otimes\mathcal{O}(-g-4)\otimes\mathcal{O}(-2))&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">⊗</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em">∧</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})\otimes\wedge^{2}\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})\otimes\mathcal{O}(-g-4)\otimes\mathcal{O}(-2))&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> then <math id="S5.SS3.p14.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u(\vec{e},\vec{f})\geq\frac{g+4}{5}-16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(\vec{e},\vec{f})\geq\frac{g+4}{5}-16</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p15.1" class="ltx_p">We now prove Theorem <a href="#S1.Thmthm4" title="Theorem 1.4. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.4</span></a> to complete the <math id="S5.SS3.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=5</annotation></semantics></math> case.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#S1.Thmthm4" title="Theorem 1.4. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.4</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS3.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose <math id="S5.SS3.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i&lt;\frac{g+4}{5}-16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i&lt;\frac{g+4}{5}-16</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, by excision and Lemma <a href="#S5.Thmthm13" title="Lemma 5.13. ‣ 5.3. Degree 
          
            5 ‣ 5. The good opens and codimension bounds ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.13</span></a>, the restriction map <math id="S5.SS3.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{i}(\mathcal{H}_{5,g})\to A^{i}(\mathcal{H}_{5,g}^{\circ})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{i}(\mathcal{H}_{5,g})\to A^{i}(\mathcal{H}_{5,g}^{\circ})</annotation></semantics></math> is an isomorphism.
Hence, <math id="S5.SS3.p16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{i}(\mathcal{H}_{5,g})\to R^{i}(\mathcal{H}_{5,g}^{\circ})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{i}(\mathcal{H}_{5,g})\to R^{i}(\mathcal{H}_{5,g}^{\circ})</annotation></semantics></math> is also an isomorphism. Since <math id="S5.SS3.p16.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{5,g}^{\circ}\subseteq\mathcal{H}_{5,g}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo>⊆</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{5,g}^{\circ}\subseteq\mathcal{H}_{5,g}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, Lemma <a href="#S5.Thmthm11" title="Lemma 5.11. ‣ 5.3. Degree 
          
            5 ‣ 5. The good opens and codimension bounds ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.11</span></a> tells us that <math id="S5.SS3.p16.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{i}(\mathcal{H}_{5,g}^{\circ})=R^{i}(\mathcal{H}_{5,g}^{\circ})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{i}(\mathcal{H}_{5,g}^{\circ})=R^{i}(\mathcal{H}_{5,g}^{\circ})</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, we have shown</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{i}(\mathcal{H}_{5,g})=A^{i}(\mathcal{H}_{5,g}^{\circ})=R^{i}(\mathcal{H}_{5,g}^{\circ})=R^{i}(\mathcal{H}_{5,g}).\qed" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" lspace="0.0835em" mathvariant="italic" separator="true">∎</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{i}(\mathcal{H}_{5,g})=A^{i}(\mathcal{H}_{5,g}^{\circ})=R^{i}(\mathcal{H}_{5,g}^{\circ})=R^{i}(\mathcal{H}_{5,g}).\qed</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6. </span>Conclusion and preview of subsequent work</h2>

<div id="S6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">At this point, we have established that, for <math id="S6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\leq 5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\leq 5</annotation></semantics></math>, a large portion of the Chow ring of the (non-factoring) Hurwitz space <math id="S6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\mathrm{nf}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>nf</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\mathrm{nf}}</annotation></semantics></math> is tautological. We did so by showing that <math id="S6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\mathrm{nf}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>nf</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\mathrm{nf}}</annotation></semantics></math> is closely approximated by an open substack <math id="S6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math> which, in turn, can be realized as an open substack of a vector bundle <math id="S6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{r,d}^{\circ}=\mathcal{X}_{r,d}^{\prime}|_{\mathcal{B}_{r,d}^{\circ}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{r,d}^{\circ}=\mathcal{X}_{r,d}^{\prime}|_{\mathcal{B}_{r,d}^{\circ}}</annotation></semantics></math> over the stack <math id="S6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{r,d}^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{r,d}^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math>. By (<a href="#S5.E6" title="In 5.2. Degree 
          
            4 ‣ 5. The good opens and codimension bounds ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.6</span></a>) and (<a href="#S5.E11" title="In 5.3. Degree 
          
            5 ‣ 5. The good opens and codimension bounds ‣ Tautological classes on Low-degree Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.11</span></a>), we understand <math id="S6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\mathcal{B}_{r,d}^{\circ})\cong A^{*}(\mathcal{X}_{r,d}^{\circ})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\mathcal{B}_{r,d}^{\circ})\cong A^{*}(\mathcal{X}_{r,d}^{\circ})</annotation></semantics></math> well. First of all, we know <math id="S6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\mathcal{B}_{r,d}^{\circ})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\mathcal{B}_{r,d}^{\circ})</annotation></semantics></math> is generated by classes which pullback to the CE classes on <math id="S6.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math>; this is how we saw <math id="S6.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\circ})=R^{*}(\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\circ})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\circ})=R^{*}(\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\circ})</annotation></semantics></math>. However, we actually know a bit more: the generators we list for <math id="S6.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\mathcal{B}_{r,d}^{\circ})\cong A^{*}(\mathcal{X}_{r,d}^{\circ})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\mathcal{B}_{r,d}^{\circ})\cong A^{*}(\mathcal{X}_{r,d}^{\circ})</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy no relations in low degrees. In other words, all relations that their pullbacks to <math id="S6.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy come from performing excision on the complement of <math id="S6.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\circ}\subset\mathcal{X}_{r,d}^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo>⊂</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\circ}\subset\mathcal{X}_{r,d}^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Determining these relations will be the focus of our subsequent work <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite>. The central innovation there is to find an appropriate resolution of the complement of <math id="S6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\circ}\subset\mathcal{X}_{r,d}^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo>⊂</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\circ}\subset\mathcal{X}_{r,d}^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math>, which allows us to determine <em id="S6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">all</em> relations in degrees up to roughly <math id="S6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g/k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g/k</annotation></semantics></math>. Furthermore, we will prove that the relations we find among the restrictions of CE classes to <math id="S6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math> actually hold on <em id="S6.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">all</em> of <math id="S6.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k,g}</annotation></semantics></math>. Using the codimension bounds we established in Section 5 here, results about the structure of <math id="S6.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\circ})=R^{*}(\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\circ})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\circ})=R^{*}(\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\circ})</annotation></semantics></math> will then translate into results about the structure of <math id="S6.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\mathrm{nf}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>nf</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\mathcal{H}_{k,g}^{\mathrm{nf}})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{*}(\mathcal{H}_{k,g})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{*}(\mathcal{H}_{k,g})</annotation></semantics></math> in degrees up to roughly <math id="S6.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g/k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g/k</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
